40431710,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples. Specifically, it mentions retrospectively performed genotypic resistance tests on proviral DNA obtained from peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) and biobanked plasma at various time points, showing the emergence of resistance mutations and the replacement of resistant strains by an ancient wild-type strain.","A genotypic resistance test was carried out, which showed emergence of resistance to all the INSTIs, including BIC (Table 1). Retrospective genotypic resistance tests were performed on proviral DNA obtained from peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) of the Swiss HIV Cohort Study biobank [1] taken seven months earlier (with HIV-1 VL  < 20  copies/mL) and on biobanked plasma (with HIV-1 VL 134 copies/mL) taken four months earlier.","The paper mentions performing genotypic resistance tests on HIV-1 RNA from plasma and proviral DNA from PBMCs, indicating that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
40431710,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data. It focuses on genotypic resistance and clinical outcomes rather than providing laboratory-based drug susceptibility testing results.","This case report provides rare, well-documented insights into the development of bictegravir resistance and the rapid re-emergence of archived wild-type virus following interruption of antiretroviral therapy. Its strengths include pharmacokinetic analysis, comprehensive resistance testing, exact drug and adherence history, next-generation sequencing from HIV-1 RNA and DNA and phylogenetic analysis.","The content of the paper discusses genotypic resistance and viral load changes, but there is no mention of in vitro susceptibility assays or data."
40431710,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates. It mentions the submission of sequences to GenBank but does not list the accession numbers within the content provided.,The data that support the findings of this case report are not publicly available due to concerns regarding patient privacy and confidentiality. Data are available from the corresponding author upon reasonable request and with appropriate institutional approvals.,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates.
40431710,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The paper reports sequencing of the protease and reverse transcriptase genes. It also discusses mutations in the integrase gene, indicating that the integrase gene was analyzed for resistance mutations.","To determine whether this observation was rather a replacement of the resistant strain by an ancient archived wild-type or reversions at the specific resistance associated nucleotide positions, all available sequences of the HIV-1 protease and reverse transcriptase were compared. This phylogenetic analysis revealed that the wild-type sequence was an ancient archived virus strain, which most likely reemerged from the latent reservoir in the absence of any selective drug pressure after the treatment stopped, fully replacing the resistant strain. The direct impact INSTI RAMs on viral replication is a matter of study: the Q148H mutation alone significantly impairs viral replication by disrupting the integrase enzyme's catalytic activity, leading to reduced efficiency in the integration of viral DNA into the host genome. However, when G140S co-occurs with Q148H, it can partially compensate for this replication defect, restoring viral replication capacity closer to wild-type levels. The T97A mutation has minimal impact on replication capacity, while the specific impact of G149A on viral replication is less well characterized and warrants further investigation.","The paper discusses mutations in the protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase genes, indicating that these genes were sequenced for resistance analysis."
40431710,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,"The sequenced samples were obtained from Switzerland, as indicated by the mention of the Swiss HIV Cohort Study and the biobank from which the samples were sourced.",Retrospective genotypic resistance tests were performed on proviral DNA obtained from peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) of the Swiss HIV Cohort Study biobank [1] taken seven months earlier (with HIV-1 VL  < 20  copies/mL) and on biobanked plasma (with HIV-1 VL 134 copies/mL) taken four months earlier. We thank the patient for giving us the opportunity to publish this report and for his participation in the Swiss HIV Cohort Study over more than 30 years at the time of publication.,"The paper explicitly mentions the Swiss HIV Cohort Study, indicating that the samples were obtained from Switzerland."
40431710,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,"The sequenced samples were obtained from various years, with specific dates mentioned in the context of genotypic resistance tests. Key dates include 2006, 2022, 2023, and 2024.","Retrospective genotypic resistance tests were performed on proviral DNA obtained from peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) of the Swiss HIV Cohort Study biobank [1] taken seven months earlier (with HIV-1 VL  < 20  copies/mL) and on biobanked plasma (with HIV-1 VL 134 copies/mL) taken four months earlier. Table 1. Summary of genotypic resistance tests (on RNA or proviral DNA) and relevant mutations and selected additional plasma RNA measurements.<br>To identify potentially selected RAMs after initiation of the new drug regimen, a further genotypic resistance test was conducted two months after the start of the new antiretroviral therapy at HIV-1 RNA VL of 1590 copies/mL of plasma. The result again showed only the wild-type virus. On July 2023, the VL decreased below 20 copies/mL after a few months on FTR, DRV/r, TAF, FTC, and ETR and DRV levels were within therapeutic ranges. A genotypic resistance test was not done.",The paper provides a timeline of key events and resistance tests indicating that samples were obtained over these years.
40431710,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The paper mentions the use of next-generation sequencing (NGS) for genotypic resistance testing. This indicates that NGS was the method employed for sequencing the HIV genomes.,"At the next follow-up two months later, the HIV-1 VL had increased to 106,000 copies/mL, CD4+ cells were 566 cells/μL. A genotypic resistance test [3] using next generation sequencing showed a complete ""wild type"" for all RAMs with a sensitivity cut-off of 1.5% at a minimum depth of 1750 reads.","The paper specifically mentions the use of next-generation sequencing for genotypic resistance tests, indicating the method used for sequencing."
40431710,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the paper does not mention that samples were cloned prior to sequencing. It discusses the use of next-generation sequencing and genotypic resistance tests without mentioning cloning of samples.","At the next follow-up two months later, the HIV-1 VL had increased to 106,000 copies/mL, CD4+ cells were 566 cells/μL. A genotypic resistance test [3] using next generation sequencing showed a complete ""wild type"" for all RAMs with a sensitivity cut-off of 1.5% at a minimum depth of 1750 reads.",The paper does not mention that samples were cloned prior to sequencing. It discusses the use of next-generation sequencing and genotypic resistance tests without mentioning cloning of samples.
40431710,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,The paper reports sequencing of HIV-1 RNA from plasma and proviral DNA from peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs).,"A genotypic resistance test was carried out, which showed emergence of resistance to all the INSTIs, including BIC (Table 1). Retrospective genotypic resistance tests were performed on proviral DNA obtained from peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) of the Swiss HIV Cohort Study biobank [1] taken seven months earlier (with HIV-1 VL  < 20  copies/mL) and on biobanked plasma (with HIV-1 VL 134 copies/mL) taken four months earlier.",The paper specifies that genotypic resistance tests were performed on HIV-1 RNA from plasma and proviral DNA from PBMCs.
40431710,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, the paper discusses sequences obtained from an individual with virological failure on a treatment regimen. It describes the emergence of resistance mutations following virological failure on a quadruple regimen including bictegravir and doravirine.","We describe a rare case of virological failure on a quadruple therapy with BIC/3TC/TAF and DOR in a treatment-experienced patient. Close monitoring of the HIV-1 VL after three weeks showed a still elevated viral load of 217 copies/mL. A genotypic resistance test was carried out, which showed emergence of resistance to all the INSTIs, including BIC (Table 1).",The paper describes the emergence of resistance mutations in an individual who experienced virological failure on a specific treatment regimen.
40431710,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"Yes, the paper mentions that the patient was enrolled in the Swiss HIV Cohort Study and participated in the TMC-125 trial, indicating that some aspects of the patient's treatment were part of a clinical trial.","In 2003, in the context of the TMC-125 trial, ART was switched to didanosine (ddI), abacavir (ABC), tenofovir disoproxil (TDF), lopinavir/ritonavir (LPV/r), and etravirine (ETR).","The paper mentions the patient's enrollment in the Swiss HIV Cohort Study and participation in the TMC-125 trial, indicating that they were part of a clinical trial."
40431710,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,"The paper focuses on a single case study of one individual, indicating that samples were obtained from this one patient for HIV sequencing.","We describe a rare case of virological failure on a quadruple therapy with BIC/3TC/TAF and DOR in a treatment-experienced patient. A 27-year-old male was diagnosed with HIV-1 infection Subtype B in 1994. At that time, he was enrolled in the Swiss HIV Cohort Study [1].","The paper is a case report focusing on one individual, so the samples were obtained from this single patient."
40431710,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from an individual who had previously received multiple antiretroviral (ARV) drugs. The patient described in the study is treatment-experienced and had received various ARV drugs over the years.","A treatment-experienced, highly adherent person living with HIV for over 25 years developed resistance mutations against all four major ART classes, including bictegravir (BIC). This led to viral failure on a quadruple regimen including BIC and doravirine (DOR).",The paper discusses a treatment-experienced individual who had been on multiple ARV regimens over the years.
40431710,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The individual in the study received NRTIs, NNRTIs, PIs, and INSTIs before sample sequencing. The paper discusses the evolution of resistance across these drug classes over time.","Zidovudine (AZT) and ritonavir (RTV) were initiated about a year later. In 1996, due to never having reached a suppressed plasma viral load, a first genotypic resistance test on HIV-1 plasma RNA was performed. In 2003, in the context of the TMC-125 trial, ART was switched to didanosine (ddI), abacavir (ABC), tenofovir disoproxil (TDF), lopinavir/ritonavir (LPV/r), and etravirine (ETR). This combination of drugs again failed to achieve viral suppression, as did the combination ddI/ABC/TDF and atazanavir/ritonavir (ATV/r) in 2005. From then on, HIV-1 VL was fully suppressed below the limit of quantification of 50 copies/mL plasma, withCD4+ cell counts ranging from 690 cells/μL to 720 cells/μL. Treatment adherence was consistently reported to be optimal [2]. A DNA-based genotypic resistance assay on proviral DNA in 2015, within the framework of the Clinical Trial CN518, revealed the additional emergence of the NRTI resistance mutation M184V. This led the treating team to discontinue AZT/3TC, while continuing TDF. At the same time, RAL was replaced by the meanwhile available dolutegravir (DTG) to strengthen the genetic resistance barrier. Two years later, in 2017, the therapy was switched to tenofovir alafenamide, emtricitabine, elvitegravir, in a single tablet regimen with the booster cobicistat (TAF/FTC/ELV/c) and DRV.",The paper details the various ARV drugs across multiple drug classes that the individual received over the course of treatment.
40431710,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The individual in the study received a variety of ARV drugs over the years, including zidovudine, ritonavir, didanosine, abacavir, tenofovir disoproxil, lopinavir/ritonavir, etravirine, raltegravir, tenofovir alafenamide, emtricitabine, elvitegravir, darunavir, bictegravir, and doravirine.","Zidovudine (AZT) and ritonavir (RTV) were initiated about a year later. In 2003, in the context of the TMC-125 trial, ART was switched to didanosine (ddI), abacavir (ABC), tenofovir disoproxil (TDF), lopinavir/ritonavir (LPV/r), and etravirine (ETR). This combination of drugs again failed to achieve viral suppression, as did the combination ddI/ABC/TDF and atazanavir/ritonavir (ATV/r) in 2005. From then on, HIV-1 VL was fully suppressed below the limit of quantification of 50 copies/mL plasma, withCD4+ cell counts ranging from 690 cells/μL to 720 cells/μL. Treatment adherence was consistently reported to be optimal [2]. A DNA-based genotypic resistance assay on proviral DNA in 2015, within the framework of the Clinical Trial CN518, revealed the additional emergence of the NRTI resistance mutation M184V. This led the treating team to discontinue AZT/3TC, while continuing TDF. At the same time, RAL was replaced by the meanwhile available dolutegravir (DTG) to strengthen the genetic resistance barrier. Two years later, in 2017, the therapy was switched to tenofovir alafenamide, emtricitabine, elvitegravir, in a single tablet regimen with the booster cobicistat (TAF/FTC/ELV/c) and DRV.",The paper lists specific ARV drugs that were part of the individual's treatment regimens over the years.
40431710,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"No, the paper states that the data supporting the findings are not publicly available due to concerns regarding patient privacy and confidentiality.",The data that support the findings of this case report are not publicly available due to concerns regarding patient privacy and confidentiality. Data are available from the corresponding author upon reasonable request and with appropriate institutional approvals.,The paper explicitly states that the data are not publicly available due to privacy concerns.
40431742,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina.","""This study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina, ensuring systematic testing of all collected samples.""","The paper mentions that genotype results were gathered from plasma samples drawn from patients, indicating that HIV sequences were reported."
40431742,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the study does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","""Susceptibility to NNRTIs was evaluated using the HIVdb Program with Stanford and ANRS criteria. Results: Samples from 1667 PLWHA were analyzed: 81.2% were male, with 52.6% identifying as men who have sex with men. According to the WHO list, the overall TDR was 12.1% (n = 203). The prevalence of RAMs was 10.1% (170/1667) for NNRTIs, 4% (67/1667) for nucleoside reverse-transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs), and 1.7% (30/1667) for protease inhibitors (PIs). The most frequent NNRTI mutations were K103N (5.6%), G190A (0.89%), and K103S (0.77%). The prevalence of DOR RAMs was <2%, with the most common being Y188L (0.53%). Rilpivirine RAM prevalence was 6%. Susceptibility to DOR, RPV, efavirenz, and nevirapine as given by the Stanford algorithm was 97.4%, 92%, 91.4%, and 90.4%, respectively. The ANRS criteria yielded susceptibility rates of 98.3%, 93.3%, 92.3%, and 90.8%, respectively.""",The paper focuses on the prevalence of resistance mutations and does not mention any in vitro susceptibility testing.
40431742,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.,The paper does not mention GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.,The paper does not include any reference to GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
40431742,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,The study sequenced the protease and reverse-transcriptase regions of the HIV-1 pol gene.,"""The amplified PCR product was 1084 base pairs in length, encompassing the protease and reverse-transcriptase regions of the HIV-1 pol gene. This fragment length provided sufficient coverage for comprehensive identification of resistance-associated mutations in both the protease and reverse-transcriptase genes.""",The paper describes the amplification and sequencing of the protease and reverse-transcriptase regions of the HIV-1 pol gene.
40431742,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from Argentina.,"""This study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina.""","The study was conducted in Buenos Aires, Argentina, and the samples were collected from two reference HIV-clinics in this region."
40431742,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The samples were collected between 2017 and 2021.,"The study was a retrospective cross-sectional, non-interventional study, conducted over the period 2017-09/2021. The study was conducted using only structured secondary data. Samples from ART-naive PLWHA were retrospectively analyzed for RAMS associated with resistance to DOR and other drugs at a reference laboratory (Laboratorio Dr. Stamboulian).",The study period is clearly mentioned as 2017 to 2021.
40431742,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The sequencing was performed using an Applied Biosystems/Hitachi 3500 Genetic Analyzer.,"The sequencing products were analyzed on an Applied Biosystems/Hitachi 3500 Genetic Analyzer (Waltham, MA, USA).",The paper specifies that the sequencing products were analyzed on an Applied Biosystems/Hitachi 3500 Genetic Analyzer.
40431742,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the samples were not cloned prior to sequencing.","""The amplified PCR products were sequenced using four primers. The sequencing products were analyzed on an Applied Biosystems/Hitachi 3500 Genetic Analyzer (Waltham, MA, USA).""","The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing, indicating direct sequencing of PCR products."
40431742,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma samples were sequenced.,"""This study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina.""",The study specifies that genotype results were gathered from plasma samples.
40431742,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"No, the study focused on treatment-naive individuals.","""Samples from ART-naive PLWHA were retrospectively analyzed for RAMS associated with resistance to DOR and other drugs at a reference laboratory (Laboratorio Dr. Stamboulian).""","The paper mentions that the samples were from ART-naïve PLWHA, indicating that there were no sequences from individuals with virological failure."
40431742,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the study was not conducted as a clinical trial.","""This study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina.""","The paper describes a cross-sectional study using routine clinical practice data, not a clinical trial."
40431742,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,Samples from 1667 individuals were analyzed.,"""Samples from 1667 PLWHA were analyzed: 81.2% were male, with 52.6% identifying as men who have sex with men. According to the WHO list, the overall TDR was 12.1% (n = 203).""",The paper states that samples from 1667 PLWHA were analyzed for drug resistance mutations.
40431742,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"No, the study focused on treatment-naive individuals.","""Samples from ART-naive PLWHA were retrospectively analyzed for RAMS associated with resistance to DOR and other drugs at a reference laboratory (Laboratorio Dr. Stamboulian).""","The paper mentions that the samples were from ART-naïve PLWHA, indicating that none had previously received ARV drugs."
40431742,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"No, the study focused on drug-naïve individuals.","""Samples from ART-naive PLWHA were retrospectively analyzed for RAMS associated with resistance to DOR and other drugs at a reference laboratory (Laboratorio Dr. Stamboulian).""","The paper specifies that the study included ART-naïve individuals, so no drug classes were received prior to sample sequencing."
40431742,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"No, the study focused on drug-naïve individuals.",Samples from ART-naive PLWHA were retrospectively analyzed for RAMS associated with resistance to DOR and other drugs at a reference laboratory (Laboratorio Dr. Stamboulian).,"The paper specifies that the study included ART-naïve individuals, so no specific drugs were received prior to sample sequencing."
40431742,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"No, the paper does not mention that the sequences were made publicly available.","""The datasets generated and/or analyzed during the current study are available from the corresponding author(s) on reasonable request.""","The paper states that the datasets are available from the corresponding authors on reasonable request, but does not mention public availability of sequences."
40490983,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reported HIV sequences from patient samples as it mentioned the sequences were analyzed and resistance mutations were obtained from sequences requested from laboratories.","Sanger sequencing of plasma HIV-1 RNA was performed by the Kisumu Kenya Medical Research Institute and Nairobi National HIV Reference Laboratories [32, 33]. Protease and reverse transcriptase resistance mutations were obtained from sequences requested from laboratories.","The methods section indicates that sequencing was performed on patient samples, confirming this point."
40490983,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data; it focuses on genotypic resistance data and clinical outcomes.","We assessed resistance prevalence and patterns at second-line VF, stratified by PI (atazanavir/ritonavir or lopinavir/ritonavir), and examined correlations of resistance and treatment strategies with VF at 6-18 months post-genotype.",The focus on prevalence and patterns of resistance without mention of specific susceptibility assays indicates a lack of in vitro data.
40490983,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates are not reported in the provided text.,No GenBank accession numbers are provided in the methods or results sections of the provided text.,The absence of GenBank accession numbers in the paper suggests they were not reported.
40490983,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,The genes sequenced include protease and reverse transcriptase as indicated by the resistance mutations analyzed in those genes.,Protease and reverse transcriptase resistance mutations were obtained from sequences requested from laboratories.,The mention of analyzing mutations specifically in the protease and reverse transcriptase genes confirms their sequencing.
40490983,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,"The sequenced samples were obtained from Kenya, specifically through the Academic Model Providing Access to Healthcare in western Kenya.","we analysed medical records from PLWH at the Academic Model Providing Access to Healthcare (AMPATH) in western Kenya, which provides guidelines-based HIV services.","The study's setting in Kenya is clearly stated, indicating the origin of the samples."
40490983,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from 2011 to 2021.,"A total of 254 second-line failure genotypes were ordered at AMPATH from 2011 to 2021. Of these, 60 were unretrievable or unverified and seven were done for children ≤3 years old. Thus, 187 PLWH with genotypes were analysed, with a median age at genotyping 41 years and 54% female (Table 1). The median genotyping year was 2017, earliest in 2011 (before Resistance Clinic started in 2015) and latest in 2021",These dates are explicitly mentioned in the study timeline.
40490983,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing was used for sequencing the HIV samples.,Sanger sequencing of plasma HIV-1 RNA was performed by the Kisumu Kenya Medical Research Institute and Nairobi National HIV Reference Laboratories.,"The methods section specifies Sanger sequencing as the technique used, confirming this point."
40490983,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the samples were not cloned prior to sequencing.",No cloning of samples is mentioned or implied in the methodology; direct sequencing of plasma RNA is mentioned as the method used.,"The methodology does not mention cloning, indicating that this step was not performed."
40490983,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma HIV-1 RNA samples were sequenced.,Sanger sequencing of plasma HIV-1 RNA was performed by the Kisumu Kenya Medical Research Institute and Nairobi National HIV Reference Laboratories.,The mention of plasma HIV-1 RNA confirms the type of clinical specimens sequenced.
40490983,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, the sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen.","We conducted a retrospective cohort study of people living with HIV (PLWH) ≥3 years old with second-line viral failure (VF, ≥1000 copies/ml) at the Academic Model Providing Access to Healthcare from 2011 to 2021.","The study specifically included individuals with second-line failure, indicating virological failure."
40490983,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the patients were not in a clinical trial; the study was a retrospective cohort study.","In this retrospective cohort study, we analysed medical records from PLWH at the Academic Model Providing Access to Healthcare (AMPATH) in western Kenya, which provides guidelines-based HIV services [29].",The retrospective nature of the study suggests that the patients were not part of a clinical trial.
40490983,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,A total of 187 individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing.,"Thus, 187 PLWH with genotypes were analysed, with a median age at genotyping 41 years and 54% female (Table 1).",This number is explicitly stated in the results section.
40490983,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","A total of 254 second-line failure genotypes were ordered at AMPATH from 2011 to 2021 (Figure 1). Most (171/187, 91%) participants had resistance at second-line failure: 79% NRTI (most common M184V-73%), 80% NNRTI (most common K103N-29%) and 37% major PI (most common M46I-27%) (Table 2 and Figure S2). Dual- (36%) or triple- (37%) class resistance was present in 73% of participants. NRTI and NNRTI mutation frequencies were similar among those on atazanavir/ritonavir versus lopinavir/ritonavir. However, more major PI mutations were detected upon atazanavir/ritonavir versus lopinavir/ritonavir VF (54% versus 26%) and certain mutations (150L/V and I84V) differed.","The study included participants with second-line failure, indicating prior ARV drug exposure."
40490983,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Individuals received NRTI, NNRTI, and PI drug classes before sample sequencing; dual-class and triple-class resistance were also reported","Of 187 participants (median age 41 years, 54% female, 41% on atazanavir/ritonavir, 59% on lopinavir/ritonavir-based ART), 91% had any resistance (NRTI 79%, NNRTI 80%, major PI 37%, dual-class 36%, triple-class 37%).",The presence of resistance mutations from these classes indicates prior treatment with these drugs.
40490983,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The drugs received included atazanavir/ritonavir, lopinavir/ritonavir, lamivudine, tenofovir, nevirapine, and zidovudine, abacavir","Table 1. Characteristics of participants at genotyping performed upon second-line failure Abbreviations: 3TC, lamivudine; ABC, abacavir; ART, antiretroviral therapy; ATV/r, atazanavir/ritonavir; EFV, efavirenz; LPV/r, lopinavir/ritonavir; NNRTI, non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor; NVP, nevirapine; PI, protease inhibitor; TDF, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate.",The presence of specific drugs and their combinations in participant regimens indicates prior ARV drug exposure.
40490983,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"No, the sequences were not made publicly available; the data availability statement does not mention this.",The data that support the findings of this study are available from the corresponding author upon reasonable request.,"The data availability statement indicates that access to the data is possible but not public, confirming this point."
40573423,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the study included HIV sequences from patient samples, specifically 487 antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naïve individuals in South Korea from 2021 to 2024.","In this study, we investigated the proportion of transmitted drug resistance (TDR) mutations and human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-1 subtypes among 487 antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naïve individuals in South Korea from 2021 to 2024 to inform more effective treatment strategies.","The evidence clearly states that the study involved sequenced samples from patients, indicating that sequences were reported."
40573423,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data; it focuses on transmitted drug resistance mutations and genetic diversity among patient samples.","In this study, we investigated the proportion of transmitted drug resistance (TDR) mutations and human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-1 subtypes among 487 antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naïve individuals in South Korea from 2021 to 2024 to inform more effective treatment strategies.",The focus on transmitted drug resistance mutations suggests an analysis of susceptibility based on observed mutations rather than in vitro testing.
40573423,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates are not provided in the abstract or materials and methods of the paper.,No specific GenBank accession numbers are mentioned in the provided text or abstract.,The paper does not include relevant information regarding GenBank accession numbers.
40573423,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The genes sequenced include the envelope (env), gag, and pol proteins for genotyping and the protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase genes for drug resistance analysis.","Reverse transcription and nested PCR were performed to amplify the envelope (env), gag protein (gag), and pol protein (pol) for genotyping and the protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase genes for drug resistance analysis.",The paper mentions specific genes that were sequenced.
40573423,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,"The sequenced samples were obtained from South Korea, with a significant portion from non-Korean individuals primarily from Asia and the Americas.","In South Korea, HIV confirmatory testing is conducted by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency (KDCA) and 17 provincial Institutes of Health and Environment. Demographic data were obtained from the Division of HIV/AIDS Prevention and Control at the KDCA. Recently diagnosed PWH who had not been exposed to ART were included. The initial diagnosis for all included PWH was made between January 2021 and October 2024. The countries of origin for non-Koreans were primarily in Asia and the Americas or were unspecified. Table 2 summarizes the demographic information for the PWH.",The population study is limited to South Korea.
40573423,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from the years 2021 to 2024.,"The study included 487 PWH: 99 from 2021, 143 from 2022, 148 from 2023, and 97 from 2024.",The paper lists the years during which samples were collected.
40573423,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing was performed using in-house sequencing primers.,Sanger sequencing was performed using in-house sequencing primers (Table 1).,The paper explicitly states that Sanger sequencing was used.
40573423,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the paper does not mention that samples were cloned prior to sequencing.",No evidence regarding cloning of samples is provided in the paper.,The paper does not provide any evidence that samples were cloned.
40573423,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Viral RNA was extracted from plasma or serum samples.,"Viral RNA was extracted from 140 μL of plasma or serum using the QIAcube extraction system (QIAGEN, Hilden, Germany), according to the manufacturer&#x27;s instructions.",The paper specifies that plasma or serum samples were used.
40573423,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"No, the study focused on antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naïve individuals, so sequences from individuals with virological failure were not included.","In this study, we investigated the proportion of transmitted drug resistance (TDR) mutations and human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-1 subtypes among 487 antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naïve individuals in South Korea from 2021 to 2024 to inform more effective treatment strategies.","The paper focused on ART-naïve individuals, meaning they had not previously received treatment, which rules out virological failure."
40573423,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the paper does not indicate that the patients were part of a clinical trial.",No evidence regarding clinical trials is provided in the paper.,The paper does not mention any clinical trial involvement.
40573423,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,Samples were obtained from 487 individuals for HIV sequencing.,"The study included 487 PWH: 99 from 2021, 143 from 2022, 148 from 2023, and 97 from 2024.",The paper states the total number of individuals from whom samples were collected.
40573423,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"No, the paper focused on antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naïve individuals, so it does not report sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","In this study, we investigated the proportion of transmitted drug resistance (TDR) mutations and human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-1 subtypes among 487 antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naïve individuals in South Korea from 2021 to 2024 to inform more effective treatment strategies.",The paper specifically focused on ART-naïve individuals.
40573423,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The study included ART-naïve individuals, so no drug classes were received before sample sequencing.","In this study, we investigated the proportion of transmitted drug resistance (TDR) mutations and human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-1 subtypes among 487 antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naïve individuals in South Korea from 2021 to 2024 to inform more effective treatment strategies.","The paper does not provide information on drug classes received, as the individuals were treatment-naïve."
40573423,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The study included ART-naïve individuals, so no specific drugs were received before sample sequencing.","In this study, we investigated the proportion of transmitted drug resistance (TDR) mutations and human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-1 subtypes among 487 antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naïve individuals in South Korea from 2021 to 2024 to inform more effective treatment strategies.","The paper does not mention any drugs received, as the individuals had not received treatment."
40573423,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"No, the paper does not mention that the sequences were made publicly available.",The data used to support this study are available from the corresponding author upon request.,The paper states that the data are available upon request but does not indicate public availability of sequences.
40596906,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the study includes genotypic sequences of HIV-1 from mother-child pairs.","This study included 15 mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1. The genotyping sequences were provided by the Brazilian Ministry of Health. Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health.","The paper explicitly mentions that genotypic sequences of HIV-1 were obtained from mother-child pairs, indicating that patient samples were used for sequencing."
40596906,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","Methods This study included 15 mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1. The genotyping sequences were provided by the Brazilian Ministry of Health. The analyses included descriptions of antiretroviral resistance mutation profiles of the mothers and children, subtype determination, and phylogenetic analyses.","The paper focuses on genotypic resistance mutations and phylogenetic analysis, without mentioning any in vitro susceptibility testing."
40596906,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates are PV526713-PV526742.,"Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health (GenBank accession number PV526713-PV526742).",The paper provides the specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates in the methods section.
40596906,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The HIV pol region, specifically the protease and reverse transcriptase (PR/RT) genes, were sequenced.","Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health.","The paper mentions that the genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region, which includes the PR and RT genes, were obtained."
40596906,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from Brazil.,"This study aimed to describe the transmission of drug-resistant HIV-1 variants and phylogenetic characterisation of viral strains in mother-child pairs from the cities of Recife and São Luís, located in the Northeast region of Brazil, in 2007–2022.","The paper clearly states that the study was conducted in Brazil, specifically in the cities of Recife and São Luís."
40596906,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from 2007 to 2022.,"This study aimed to describe the transmission of drug-resistant HIV-1 variants and phylogenetic characterisation of viral strains in mother-child pairs from the cities of Recife and São Luís, located in the Northeast region of Brazil, in 2007–2022.","The paper mentions the time period during which the samples were collected, which is from 2007 to 2022."
40596906,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The ViroSeq Genotyping System was used for sequencing.,"Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health.",The paper specifies the use of the ViroSeq Genotyping System for obtaining genotypic sequences.
40596906,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the paper does not mention that samples were cloned prior to sequencing.","This study included 15 mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1. The genotyping sequences were provided by the Brazilian Ministry of Health. The analyses included descriptions of antiretroviral resistance mutation profiles of the mothers and children, subtype determination, and phylogenetic analyses. Data were obtained from secondary sources, including medical records from hospital and outpatient services where patients were followed. Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health. The genotyping sequences were provided by the Brazilian Ministry of Health",Paper does not mention the cloning of samples before sequencing.
40596906,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Clinical samples from mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1 were sequenced.,"This study included 15 mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1. Data were obtained from secondary sources, including medical records from hospital and outpatient services where patients were followed.",The paper states that the study included mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1.
40596906,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, some mothers in the study had virological failure and required genotyping.",The mothers included both treatment-naive women diagnosed during pregnancy who underwent pretreatment genotyping and those living with HIV-1 during prior treatment who required genotyping due to virological failure.,The paper mentions that some mothers had virological failure and required genotyping.
40596906,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the paper does not mention that the patients were in a clinical trial.","This study was conducted from October 2021 to September 2023 in São Luís, Maranhão, and Recife, Pernambuco, at the High-Risk Maternity Hospital in Imperatriz, Pediatric Infectious Disease Outpatient Clinic at the University Hospital of the Federal University of Maranhão, and Pediatric Infectious Disease Outpatient Clinic at the University Hospital Oswaldo Cruz of the University of Pernambuco.","The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial, it describes the study as observational."
40596906,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,"Samples were obtained from 15 mother-child pairs, totaling 30 individuals.",This study included 15 mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1.,"The paper states that 15 mother-child pairs were included in the study, indicating that samples were obtained from 30 individuals."
40596906,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper includes mothers who had previously received ARV drugs.",The mothers included both treatment-naive women diagnosed during pregnancy who underwent pretreatment genotyping and those living with HIV-1 during prior treatment who required genotyping due to virological failure.,The paper mentions that some mothers were treatment-naive but others were living with HIV-1 during prior treatment.
40596906,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Individuals in the study received drugs from the NRTI and NNRTI classes.,"Seven mother-child pairs exhibited similar mutation profiles, with three showing no mutations and four displaying similar resistance mutations to the nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI) and non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI) drug classes. Mutations conferring resistance to efavirenz, nevirapine, lamivudine, abacavir, and didanosine were frequently observed in children and mothers.","The paper discusses the mutations observed in NRTI and NNRTI drug classes, indicating that these drugs were received."
40596906,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Individuals received zidovudine (ZDV), lamivudine (3TC), nevirapine (NVP), lopinavir/ritonavir, and efavirenz (EFV).","Of the children, eight (53%) were male, and 10 (66.7%) started ART within the first 2 years of life. In one case (6.7%), no record of ART initiation was found. Nine children (60%) had initiated ART, including zidovudine (ZDV) + lamivudine (3TC) + nevirapine (NVP) in three (20%), ZDV + 3TC + lopinavir/ritonavir in two (13.3%), and ZDV + 3TC + efavirenz (EFV) in two (6.7%), while no treatment was described for three (20%). Mother-child pairs 1, 2, 5, and 7 received the same ART regimen (ZDV + 3TC + NVP). Mothers 3, 6, 8, 9, and 15 received EFV-based regimens.",The paper lists specific drugs that were part of the ART regimens received by the mother-child pairs.
40596906,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"Yes, the GenBank accession numbers provided indicate that the sequences were made publicly available.","Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health (GenBank accession number PV526713-PV526742).","The paper provides GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, indicating that they were made publicly available."
40713598,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples. Specifically, genotypic drug resistance testing of stored samples from the 96 individuals with HIV-1 RNA >1,000 copies/ml was attempted, and 20 samples were successfully amplified and sequenced.","Genotypic drug resistance testing of stored samples from the 96 individuals with HIV-1 RNA >1,000 copies/ml was attempted. Twenty samples were successfully amplified and sequenced.",The evidence clearly states that sequencing was performed on patient samples with specific criteria.
40713598,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data. It focuses on genotypic drug resistance profiles and treatment outcomes based on previous ART regimens and observed resistance.","HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) was retrospectively characterized among 20 children and adolescents with HIV with virologic failure on non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI)-based therapy, and virologic response in those switched to dolutegravir (DTG)-based therapy described. All participants had at least one NNRTI resistance mutation, most commonly K103N (N = 12) and 15 (75%) had nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI) resistance mutations, most commonly M184I/V (N = 15) . Five (45%) of 11 participants who were switched to DTG-based regimens for a median of 50 months had HIV suppression. Further studies to understand the role of pre-existing HIVDR in the failure of DTG-based regimens are needed.","The focus of the paper is on genotypic resistance and treatment outcomes, not on in vitro susceptibility assays."
40713598,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The GenBank accession numbers are not provided in the content of the paper. The study did not mention any accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.,No datasets were generated or analysed during the current study.,"The paper explicitly states there were no datasets generated, implying no GenBank accession numbers."
40713598,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The HIV-1 pol gene was sequenced, encompassing the protease (PR) and reverse transcriptase (RT) regions.","The HIV-1 pol gene, which was amplified and sequenced in this study, encompasses the protease (PR) and reverse transcriptase (RT) regions.","The evidence directly states that the pol gene, including PR and RT, was sequenced in the study."
40713598,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,"The sequenced samples were obtained from Ghana, specifically from the Pediatric HIV/AIDS Care Program at Korle-Bu Teaching Hospital in Ghana.",Participants included CAWH from a previous study that examined the virologic response to NNRTI-based ART from the Pediatric HIV/AIDS Care Program at Korle-Bu Teaching Hospital in Ghana.,The evidence indicates that the samples were specifically from a program in Ghana.
40713598,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The specific years from which the sequenced samples were obtained are not mentioned in the paper.,No specific years for sample collection are provided in the content of the paper.,The paper does not provide any information regarding the years of sample collection.
40713598,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Next-generation sequencing (NGS) was conducted on the Illumina MiSeq platform.,"HIV-1 pol was amplified using two-round PCR, and next-generation sequencing (NGS) was conducted on the Illumina MiSeq platform following previously published protocols.",The evidence mentions the use of NGS on the Illumina MiSeq platform for sequencing.
40713598,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the samples were not cloned prior to sequencing. The paper does not mention any cloning of samples.",The study does not mention that samples were cloned prior to sequencing.,The paper does not provide any information regarding the cloning of samples before sequencing.
40713598,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Frozen plasma samples were used for sequencing.,"Briefly, frozen plasma samples were shipped on dry ice to the Virology Quality Assurance-approved laboratory at the Providence-Boston Center for AIDS Research Laboratory.",The evidence indicates that plasma samples were the clinical specimens sequenced.
40713598,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, the paper reports sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen. It specifically focuses on children and adolescents with virologic failure on NNRTI-based therapy.","All participants had at least one NNRTI resistance mutation, most commonly K103N (N = 12) and 15 (75%) had nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI) resistance mutations, most commonly M184I/V (N = 15). HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) was retrospectively characterized among 20 children and adolescents with HIV with virologic failure on non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI)-based therapy, and virologic response in those switched to dolutegravir (DTG)-based therapy described.",The evidence indicates that samples were from individuals who had virologic failure.
40713598,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial.",Participants included CAWH from a previous study that examined the virologic response to NNRTI-based ART from the Pediatric HIV/AIDS Care Program at Korle-Bu Teaching Hospital in Ghana,The content focuses on retrospective data and does not mention a clinical trial.
40713598,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,"Samples were attempted from 96 individuals with HIV-1 RNA >1,000 copies/ml, but 20 samples were successfully amplified and sequenced.","Genotypic drug resistance testing of stored samples from the 96 individuals with HIV-1 RNA >1,000 copies/ml was attempted. Twenty samples were successfully amplified and sequenced.",The evidence states that samples were from 96 individuals but only 20 were successfully sequenced.
40713598,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs. It discusses resistance in children and adolescents on NNRTI-based antiretroviral therapy.","HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) was retrospectively characterized among 20 children and adolescents with HIV with virologic failure on non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI)-based therapy, and virologic response in those switched to dolutegravir (DTG)-based therapy described. All participants had at least one NNRTI resistance mutation, most commonly K103N (N = 12) and 15 (75%) had nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI) resistance mutations, most commonly M184I/V (N = 15).",The paper mentioned the participants switched to DTG-based ART after being on NNRTI-based therapy.
40713598,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Individuals in the study received non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NNRTIs) and nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs) before sample sequencing.,"HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) was retrospectively characterized among 20 children and adolescents with HIV with virologic failure on non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI)-based therapy, and 15 (75%) had nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI) resistance mutations, most commonly M184I/V (N = 15).",The evidence indicates that patients were on NNRTI-based therapy and had NRTI resistance.
40713598,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Specific drugs received by individuals included nevirapine, efavirenz, lamivudine, tenofovir, abacavir, and zidovudine before sample sequencing.",Table 1 Clinical and drug resistance data of 20 the participants,The evidence lists specific drugs that were part of the ART regimens prior to sequencing.
40713598,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"No, the paper does not mention that the sequences were made publicly available.",No datasets were generated or analysed during the current study.,"The evidence suggests that no datasets, including sequences, were made publicly available."
40763144,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"No, the paper does not report HIV sequences from patient samples.","We estimated the prevalence of HIV drug resistance, described the HIV drug resistance mutations and evaluated the factors associated with HIVDR among PLHIV with virological failure in the West-Nile region of Uganda.","The focus of the study was on the prevalence and characteristics of HIV drug resistance mutations, but it did not mention sequencing of HIV samples."
40763144,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","We estimated the prevalence of HIV drug resistance, described the HIV drug resistance mutations and evaluated the factors associated with HIVDR among PLHIV with virological failure in the West-Nile region of Uganda.",The study focused on the prevalence and characteristics of HIV drug resistance mutations rather than in vitro drug susceptibility testing.
40763144,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates.,"We estimated the prevalence of HIV drug resistance, described the HIV drug resistance mutations and evaluated the factors associated with HIVDR among PLHIV with virological failure in the West-Nile region of Uganda.",The study did not mention any sequenced HIV isolates or corresponding GenBank accession numbers.
40763144,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,The paper does not report the sequencing of specific HIV genes.,"We estimated the prevalence of HIV drug resistance, described the HIV drug resistance mutations and evaluated the factors associated with HIVDR among PLHIV with virological failure in the West-Nile region of Uganda.",The study focused on the prevalence and characteristics of HIV drug resistance mutations without detailing specific genes sequenced.
40763144,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The paper does not mention sequenced samples from any country.,"We estimated the prevalence of HIV drug resistance, described the HIV drug resistance mutations and evaluated the factors associated with HIVDR among PLHIV with virological failure in the West-Nile region of Uganda.","The focus was on Uganda, and no other countries were mentioned regarding sample collection."
40763144,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The paper does not provide information on the years from which sequenced samples were obtained.,"All PLHIV, regardless of age, who had been on ART for at least one year, experienced virological failure and underwent an HIVDR test between 1st January 2021– 30th December 2023 were included in the study. Demographic and clinical data were extracted from the National HIVDR database.",The study did  not mention any sequenced samples or the years they were collected.
40763144,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The study used Sanger sequencing or Next Generation Sequencing.,"Sequencing, where individual mutations are identified using either Sanger sequencing or Next generation sequencing is then carried out.",The paper mentioned the methods used to identify HIV mutations.
40763144,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,The study does not mention whether samples were cloned prior to sequencing.,"Study design and participants We conducted a retrospective cross-sectional study in the West-Nile region of Uganda across the 161 health facilities that offer comprehensive ART services [17]. The region had a population of 3.6 million people in 2023 and an estimated 49,000 PLHIV [15]. Study participants included all PLHIV, regardless of age, who had been on ART for at least one year, had a non-suppressed HIV viral load (>1000 copies/ml) and underwent an HIVDR test between 1st January 2021– 30th December 2023.",The study focused on the prevalence of HIVDR.
40763144,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,The study used plasma or dried blood spot (DBS) samples for sequencing.,A Plasma or dried blood spot (DBS) sample is collected and referred to the HIVDR testing facility at a central national laboratory.,The paper specifies the types of specimens collected for HIVDR testing.
40763144,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, the paper reports sequences from individuals with virological failure.","Study participants included all PLHIV, regardless of age, who had been on ART for at least one year, had a non-suppressed HIV viral load (>1000 copies/ml) and underwent an HIVDR test between 1st January 2021– 30th December 2023. Demographic and clinical data were extracted from the National HIVDR database. HIVDR was defined as having at least one mutation with a penalty score of ≥15.",The study focused on individuals experiencing virological failure.
40763144,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the paper does not mention that patients were part of a clinical trial.",We conducted a retrospective cross-sectional analysis of HIVDR data in the West-Nile region of Uganda across the 161 health facilities that offer comprehensive Anti-retroviral therapy (ART) services.,"The study was a retrospective cross-sectional analysis, not a clinical trial."
40763144,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,295 individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing.,"Of these, majority were female (56.6%) and adults aged 13.0; years (49.2%). The median age was 19 (Inter quartile range [IQR]: 13-41) years, and median duration on ART was 8 (IQR: 5-10) years. Overall, 218 (73.9%) had HIVDR with 66% of subjects having Non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase (NNRTI) mutations. M184V/I (50%), K103N (34%) and TAMS (26%) were the commonest mutations. Resistance to Etravirine (27%) was higher than that of Dolutegravir (12%) and Darunavir (5%).",All participants with HIV DR results were included in the study.
40763144,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper includes participants who had previously received ARV drugs.","Study participants included all PLHIV, regardless of age, who had been on ART for at least one year, had a non-suppressed HIV viral load (>1000 copies/ml) and underwent an HIVDR test between 1st January 2021023.",The study included individuals who had been on ART for at least one year.
40763144,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Individuals received NRTIs, NNRTIs, PIs, and INSTIs before sample sequencing.",HIVDR mutations were present in 218 participants (73.9%: 95% Confidence Interval (CI) 68.9-78.9%). Majority of the participants (66%) had NNRTI mutations while 55% had NRTI mutations (Table 2).,The study reported mutations across multiple drug classes.
40763144,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Drugs received included Abacavir, Lamivudine, Zidovudine, Tenofovir, Dolutegravir, Atazanavir, Lopinavir, and Darunavir.","Demographic data included age and sex. Clinical data included viral load copies preceding the DR test, WHO clinical stage, ART regimen class at the time of sample collection, NRTI anchor drug of the regimen, the full ART regimen, duration on ART, the line of ART treatment, indication for the HIVDR test, year of HIVDR test and actual mutations per participant.",The paper mentioned the specific drugs included in the ART regimens of participants.
40763144,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"No, the sequences from the paper were not made publicly available.","The data used in this study is available on the Ugandan Ministry of Health HIV Drug Resistance Database but is not publicly accessible due to patient confidentiality policies. Access may be granted upon request to the Ugandan Ministry of Health through the Director General, Health Services.",The data was not publicly accessible due to confidentiality reasons.
40779404,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples, specifically from individuals with preexisting K65R/N mutations.",Post hoc analysis evaluating virologic outcomes in VS individuals with preexisting K65R/N mutations documented by historical genotypes and/or baseline proviral DNA sequencing who received B/F/TAF in 6 Phase 2/3/3b clinical trials.,The paper mentions the use of historical genotypes and baseline proviral DNA sequencing to document K65R/N mutations in patients.
40779404,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.",Background: Preexisting HIV-1 drug resistance affects antiretroviral treatment options for people with HIV-1 (PWH). Prior studies have demonstrated safety and efficacy of bictegravir/emtricitabine/tenofovir (TFV) alafenamide [B/F/tenofovir alafenamide fumarate (TAF)] in PWH including in virologically suppressed (VS) individuals with M184V/I mutations in reverse transcriptase that confer resistance to emtricitabine. K65R/N mutations in reverse transcriptase are selected by and confer 2-3-fold reduced susceptibility to TFV or its prodrugs TFV disoproxil fumarate (TDF) and TFV alafenamide fumarate (TAF) in vitro.,The focus of the paper is on clinical trial outcomes and historical genotypic data rather than new in vitro susceptibility testing.
40779404,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.,No evidence found.,"The paper does not mention GenBank accession numbers, indicating they were not provided."
40779404,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The HIV genes reported to have been sequenced include protease (PR), reverse transcriptase (RT), and integrase (IN).","Historical RNA or proviral DNA genotyping reports for protease (PR), RT, and integrase (IN), from local laboratories or commercial sites were collected if available.",The paper details the genotyping of these specific genes for resistance analysis.
40779404,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The paper does not specify the countries from which the sequenced samples were obtained.,No evidence found.,The paper focuses on clinical trial participants without geographical detail.
40779404,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The paper does not provide specific years from which the sequenced samples were obtained.,No evidence found.,The time frame of sample collection is not mentioned in the context of the paper.
40779404,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The sequencing method used was next-generation sequencing (NGS).,"Retrospective proviral DNA genotyping of PR/RT/IN using GenoSure Archive (Monogram Biosciences, CA), which uses NGS technology was performed on BL whole blood samples.",The paper specifies the use of NGS technology for genotyping.
40779404,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, samples were not cloned prior to sequencing.","Retrospective proviral DNA genotyping of PR/RT/IN using GenoSure Archive (Monogram Biosciences, CA), which uses NGS technology was performed on BL whole blood samples.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
40779404,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Whole blood samples were sequenced for proviral DNA.,"Post hoc analysis evaluating virologic outcomes in VS individuals with preexisting K65R/N mutations documented by historical genotypes and/or baseline proviral DNA sequencing who received B/F/TAF in 6 Phase 2/3/3b clinical trials Retrospective proviral DNA genotyping of PR/RT/IN using GenoSure Archive (Monogram Biosciences, CA), which uses NGS technology was performed on BL whole blood samples","The paper states that BL whole blood samples were genotyped, indicating the type of clinical specimens sequenced."
40779404,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"No, the paper does not report sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure.","All participants with preexisting K65R/N receiving B/F/TAF (n = 20/20) had virologic suppression (HIV-1 RNA < 50 copies/mL) through end of study, with no virologic failure or treatment-emergent resistance to B/F/TAF.",The focus is on participants who maintained virologic suppression throughout the study.
40779404,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"Yes, the patients were part of Phase 2/3/3b clinical trials.",Post hoc analysis evaluating virologic outcomes in VS individuals with preexisting K65R/N mutations documented by historical genotypes and/or baseline proviral DNA sequencing who received B/F/TAF in 6 Phase 2/3/3b clinical trials.,The paper describes a post hoc analysis of data from multiple clinical trials.
40779404,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,Samples were obtained from 2028 individuals for HIV sequencing.,"From the 2182 participants who received B/F/TAF, 2028 participants had BL genotypic RT data [1474 (n = 95), 1844 (n = 522), 1878 (n = 524), 4030 (n = 333), 4449 (n = 84), and 4580 (n = 470)], and of those, K65R/N was detected in 20/2028 (1.0%) of participants.",The paper provides the total number of participants with baseline genotypic data.
40779404,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","All participants with preexisting K65R/N were VS at study start with median time on ART before study entry of 9.2 years (range 1.6–26.3 years). Before enrollment, participants had been treated with TFV (80.0%), INSTIs (50.0%), non-nucleoside RT inhibitors (NNRTI; 45.0%), and PR inhibitors (PI; 75.0%) (Table 1. Detailed ART histories of participants with preexisting K65R/N are listed in Table 1, Supplemental Digital Content, http://links.lww.com/QAI/C557.","Participants with K65R were treated with TFV and other ARV drugs before sample collection, and ART histories of participants were provided."
40779404,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Participants received NRTIs, INSTIs, NNRTIs, and protease inhibitors (PIs) before sample sequencing.","Before enrollment, participants had been treated with TFV (80.0%), INSTIs (50.0%), non-nucleoside RT inhibitors (NNRTI; 45.0%), and PR inhibitors (PI; 75.0%) (Table 1. Detailed ART histories of participants with preexisting K65R/N are listed in Table 1, Supplemental Digital Content, http://links.lww.com/QAI/C557",The paper lists the specific drug classes that participants received prior to enrollment.
40779404,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Participants received tenofovir (TFV), INSTIs, NNRTIs, and protease inhibitors (PIs) before sample sequencing.","Before enrollment, participants had been treated with TFV (80.0%), INSTIs (50.0%), non-nucleoside RT inhibitors (NNRTI; 45.0%), and PR inhibitors (PI; 75.0%) (Table 1. Detailed ART histories of participants with preexisting K65R/N are listed in Table 1, Supplemental Digital Content, http://links.lww.com/QAI/C557","The paper provides specific details on the drugs received, including TFV and various ARV classes."
40779404,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"No, the paper does not mention whether the sequences were made publicly available.",No evidence found.,The paper does not provide information regarding the public availability of the sequences.
40839365,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples.","Among 213 participants with confirmed virologic failure, 212 samples were successfully genotyped for protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase. The study collected plasma samples for VL testing and genotypic HIVDR testing.","The paper clearly states that samples were genotyped from participants with confirmed virologic failure, indicating that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
40839365,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.",The focus of the study was on genotypic resistance and the prevalence of drug resistance mutations among samples from individuals with confirmed virologic failure. We conducted a national HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) survey in adults on DBR with high viral load (VL) results after intensive adherence counseling (IAC).,The paper emphasizes genotypic testing and analysis of resistance mutations rather than in vitro susceptibility testing data.
40839365,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not mention the GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.,There is no mention of GenBank accession numbers in the provided text.  The study does not detail any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced isolates.,The absence of this information in the paper indicates that the authors did not provide GenBank accession numbers.
40839365,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The genes sequenced were protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase.","Among 213 participants with confirmed virologic failure, 212 samples were successfully genotyped for protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase.",The paper explicitly states that these specific genes were sequenced in the study.
40839365,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from Malawi.,The study was conducted in Malawi and specifically targeted high-volume ART clinics within the country.,"The paper clearly states that the study was conducted in Malawi, indicating the origin of the samples."
40839365,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The samples were obtained between July 2022 and February 2023.,"The survey was conducted between July 2022 and February 2023. From the 25 highest volume ART clinics in Malawi, 18 were selected using simple random sampling. Procedures The study teams at each facility compiled a list of eligible PLHIV, using high-VL registers, electronic medical records, and laboratory results logbooks. A 5-mL whole venous blood sample was obtained from consenting participants for an additional VL and HIVDR testing. Clinical and demographic data of participants were abstracted from the electronic medical records. These data included age, sex, HIV and ART history, IAC sessions completed, previous VL results, details of the current ART regimen, and of any previous regimens.",The paper specifies the time frame during which the samples were collected.
40839365,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The study used Sanger sequencing for genotypic analysis.,"HIV RNA was extracted using NUCLISENS easyMAG (BioMerieux) from 200 μL of plasma, with 10 μL of extracted RNA; gene fragments of protease and reverse transcriptase and integrase were amplified and sequenced using HIV-1 Genotyping kit with Integrase and the 3500XL Genetic Analyzers (Applied Biosystems). Sanger sequence electropherograms were analyzed by using RECall (v2.32)",The paper details the laboratory procedures and the use of Sanger sequencing for analyzing the samples.
40839365,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the samples were not cloned prior to sequencing.",The study does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. Gene fragments of protease and reverse transcriptase and integrase were amplified and sequenced using HIV-1 Genotyping kit with Integrase and the 3500XL Genetic Analyzers (Applied Biosystems). Sanger sequence electropherograms were analyzed by using RECall (v2.32),The laboratory procedures described in the paper do not include any mention of cloning.
40839365,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma samples were sequenced.,"A 5-mL whole venous blood sample was obtained from consenting participants for an additional VL and HIVDR testing. Plasma was separated from the venous whole blood samples that were collected in an EDTA tube by centrifugation and aliquoted at each health facility and kept at -20°C until they were transported on dry ice to the National HIV Reference Laboratory (NHRL) in Lilongwe. At NHRL, VL was measured using the automated Abbott m2000sp/rt Real Time HIV-1 assay from 200 μL of plasma",The paper specifies that plasma samples were collected for VL testing and genotypic HIVDR testing.
40839365,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen.","We enrolled consenting adults (≥15 years), on DBR for ≥9 months, when returning for follow-up VL testing after a previous high VL (≥1000 copies/mL) and completing IAC. Among 213 participants with confirmed virologic failure, 212 samples were successfully genotyped for protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase.","The paper mentions that the study included individuals with confirmed virologic failure, indicating that sequences were obtained from these individuals."
40839365,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the patients were not in a clinical trial.","The study was a national cross-sectional survey investigating HIV drug resistance among adults on DBR in Malawi, not a clinical trial.",The paper describes the study as a cross-sectional survey rather than a clinical trial.
40839365,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,Samples were obtained from 213 individuals with confirmed virologic failure.,"Among 213 participants with confirmed virologic failure, 212 samples were successfully genotyped for protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase.",The paper states that samples were obtained from 213 individuals with confirmed virologic failure.
40839365,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","We enrolled consenting adults (≥15 years), on DBR for ≥9 months, when returning for follow-up VL testing after a previous high VL (≥1000 copies/mL) and completing IAC. Among 213 participants with confirmed virologic failure, 212 samples were successfully genotyped for protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase.","The paper details that individuals had been on DBR for at least 9 months prior to sample collection, indicating prior ARV drug exposure."
40839365,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Individuals in the study received drugs from the NRTI, NNRTI, PI, and INSTI classes before sample sequencing.","Prevalence of drug resistance mutations (DRMs) to nucleotide reverse-transcriptase inhibitors was 22.6% (95% CI: 17.4% to 27.8%), to non-nucleoside reverse-transcriptase inhibitors 55.1% (95% CI 48.2% to 62.1%), and to protease inhibitors 4.9% (95% CI 1.3% to 8.5%). Prevalence of major dolutegravir DRMs was 8.5% (95% CI 5.3% to 11.9%).","The paper lists the drug resistance mutations found across different classes, indicating the classes of drugs received."
40839365,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,The specific drugs received by individuals prior to sequencing are not listed in the provided text.,"The study mentions that details of the current ART regimen, and of any previous regimens were abstracted from the electronic medical records, but does not explicitly name the drugs received prior to sequencing. Among 213 participants with confirmed virologic failure, 212 samples were successfully genotyped for protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase. Prevalence of drug resistance mutations (DRMs) to nucleotide reverse-transcriptase inhibitors was 22.6% (95% CI: 17.4% to 27.8%), to non-nucleoside reverse-transcriptase inhibitors 55.1% (95% CI 48.2% to 62.1%), and to protease inhibitors 4.9% (95% CI 1.3% to 8.5%). Prevalence of major dolutegravir DRMs was 8.5% (95% CI 5.3% to 11.9%). DTG DRMs identified included G118R (8), E138K (8), R263K/A (5), Q148R (3), and T66A/I/V (3).","The paper does not provide specific names of drugs received, only mentions that DRMs for some drugs were detected."
40839365,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,The paper does not mention whether the sequences were made publicly available.,The study does not mention any public availability of the sequences obtained during the research.,The absence of this information indicates that the sequences were not made publicly available.
40857111,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, HIV-1 resistance results were reported based on participant samples.","""This subanalysis reports HIV-1 resistance results to the end of masked treatment (DTG+F/TDF, n = 122) and to study end (B/F/TAF, n = 119; DTG+F/TDF to B/F/TAF, n = 89).""","The paper discusses the analysis of HIV-1 resistance, indicating that sequences were obtained from patient samples."
