40857111,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Clinical samples were sequenced.,"""This subanalysis reports HIV-1 resistance results to the end of masked treatment (DTG+F/TDF, n = 122) and to study end (B/F/TAF, n = 119; DTG+F/TDF to B/F/TAF, n = 89).""",The paper discusses resistance analysis from clinical samples.
40857111,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure.","""Participants with virologic failure had postbaseline resistance testing of PR/RT/IN""",The paper mentions that participants with virological failure underwent resistance testing.
40857111,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"Yes, the study was a clinical trial.","""The design of the phase 3 randomized ALLIANCE study (GS-US-380-4458; NCT03547908) has been described previously.""",The paper mentions that the study was a phase 3 randomized clinical trial.
40857111,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,The paper mentions that data were available for at least 19 individuals.,"In total, 22 participants met the criteria for postbaseline HIV-1 resistance testing, and data were available for ≥1 gene for 19 (86%) of these participants, including 10 participants in the DTG+F/TDF group, 10 participants in the B/F/TAF group, and 2 participants in the DTG+F/TDF to B/F/TAF group.",The paper mentions that resistance data was available for 19 individuals.
40857111,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, individuals had previously received ARV drugs before sequencing.","""Background: ALLIANCE is a phase 3 randomized study of bibtegravir/emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (B/F/TAF) versus dolutegravir + emtricitabine/tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (DTG+F/TDF) in treatment-naive people with HIV-1/hepatitis B virus (HBV) coinfection. Methods: After the 96-week randomized phase of ALLIANCE, participants could enter a 48-week open-label B/F/TAF-only phase. This subanalysis reports HIV-1 resistance results to the end of masked treatment (DTG+F/TDF, n = 122) and to study end (B/F/TAF, n = 119; DTG+F/TDF to B/F/TAF, n = 89). Baseline resistance was determined using historical and screening genotypes of protease (PR), reverse transcriptase (RT), and integrase (IN), if available. Participants with virologic failure had postbaseline resistance testing of PR/RT/IN; those subsequently not achieving virologic suppression (VS; HIV-1 RNA < 50 copies/mL) were included in final resistance analysis population (RAP).""",The paper discusses participants who were on ARV drugs.
40857111,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, INSTI","Background: ALLIANCE is a phase 3 randomized study of bibtegravir/emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (B/F/TAF) versus dolutegravir + emtricitabine/tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (DTG+F/TDF) in treatment-naive people with HIV-1/hepatitis B virus (HBV) coinfection. Methods: After the 96-week randomized phase of ALLIANCE, participants could enter a 48-week open-label B/F/TAF-only phase. This subanalysis reports HIV-1 resistance results to the end of masked treatment (DTG+F/TDF, n = 122) and to study end (B/F/TAF, n = 119; DTG+F/TDF to B/F/TAF, n = 89). Baseline resistance was determined using historical and screening genotypes of protease (PR), reverse transcriptase (RT), and integrase (IN), if available. Participants with virologic failure had postbaseline resistance testing of PR/RT/IN; those subsequently not achieving virologic suppression (VS; HIV-1 RNA < 50 copies/mL) were included in final resistance analysis population (RAP).",The paper mentioned that the in study they dealt with integrase and reverse transcriptase and protease (which are all are targeted by NRTIs and INSTIs i.e DTG+F/TDF)
40857111,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Bictegravir, Emtricitabine, Tenofovir Alafenamide, Dolutegravir, Emtricitabine, Tenofovir Disoproxil Fumarate","Background: ALLIANCE is a phase 3 randomized study of bibtegravir/emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (B/F/TAF) versus dolutegravir + emtricitabine/tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (DTG+F/TDF) in treatment-naive people with HIV-1/hepatitis B virus (HBV) coinfection. Methods: After the 96-week randomized phase of ALLIANCE, participants could enter a 48-week open-label B/F/TAF-only phase. This subanalysis reports HIV-1 resistance results to the end of masked treatment (DTG+F/TDF, n = 122) and to study end (B/F/TAF, n = 119; DTG+F/TDF to B/F/TAF, n = 89). Baseline resistance was determined using historical and screening genotypes of protease (PR), reverse transcriptase (RT), and integrase (IN), if available. Participants with virologic failure had postbaseline resistance testing of PR/RT/IN; those subsequently not achieving virologic suppression (VS; HIV-1 RNA < 50 copies/mL) were included in final resistance analysis population (RAP).",The paper mentioned that the study involved drugs that belong to these drug classes.
40857111,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"No, the paper does not mention that sequences were made publicly available.",No evidence available,The content does not mention public availability of sequences.
40872801,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples.","The overall prevalence of acquired drug resistance mutations in the participants with virological failure whose samples were successfully genotyped was 87.61% (95% CI: 76.25–95.91%, I2 = 96.15%), and subgroup analysis showed a significant decline over time in the prevalence of DRMs, especially in studies that were conducted from beyond 2019.","The paper discusses the genotyping of samples from patients with virological failure, indicating that HIV sequences were reported from patient samples."
40872801,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","To inform policy, this review aimed to determine the magnitude and patterns of DRMs in patients on ART in Tanzania. A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024. A total of 9685 HIV patients from 23 eligible studies were analyzed. The prevalence of virological failure in studies that used a threshold of >1000 and >400 copies/mL was 24.83% (95% CI: 17.85-32.53%) and 36.94% (95% CI: 24.79-50.00%), respectively. Major DRMs were observed at 87.61% (95% CI: 76.25-95.91%). A decrease in prevalence was observed in studies conducted from 2019, with a pooled prevalence of 62.15% (95% CI: 31.57-88.33%).",The paper focuses on a systematic review and meta-analysis of existing studies on drug resistance mutations and HIV-1 subtypes in Tanzania does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility testing.
40872801,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates.,The systematic review protocol was registered in the International Prospective Register of Systematic Reviews (PROSPERO) on 7 January 2025 under the registration number CRD42025606698.,"The paper does not mention any specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, focusing instead on the prevalence of drug resistance mutations."
40872801,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The paper reports the sequencing of drug resistance mutations Including RT, PR, and IN genes.","Some studies followed participants longitudinally, assessing virological failure as well as DRMs prevalence, and other studies enrolled participants who already had virological failure.","The paper discusses the prevalence of drug resistance mutations in various genes, including those coding for reverse transcriptase (RT), protease (PR), and integrase (IN), indicating that these genes were sequenced."
40872801,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from Tanzania.,"A systematic literature review was conducted from February to May 2025 following PRISMA standards [11], including original studies that were conducted in Tanzania involving participants receiving ART published in English by the end of December 2024.","The paper focuses on studies conducted in Tanzania, indicating that the sequenced samples were obtained from this country."
40872801,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from studies published until the end of December 2024.,"The systematic literature search was carried out between February and March 2025 on online databases including MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL, while Google Scholar was used to identify grey literature and would not be identified by other databases. The concepts 'Drug Resistance Mutations', 'Drug Resistance', 'ART resistance', 'HIV-1 Subtypes', 'HIV Subtypes', 'HIV', and 'Tanzania' were used as key concepts alongside related search terms to construct the search strategy. Boolean operators 'AND', 'OR', and 'NOT' were used to combine different concepts, similar terms, and exclude studies","The paper does not specify the exact years from which the samples were obtained, but it mentions a systematic review of studies published up to December 2024, and other periods the studies has been carried out."
40872801,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The paper does not specify the exact method used for sequencing.,"The systematic literature search was carried out between February and March 2025 on online databases including MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL, while Google Scholar was used to identify grey literature and would not be identified by other databases. The concepts 'Drug Resistance Mutations', 'Drug Resistance', 'ART resistance', 'HIV-1 Subtypes', 'HIV Subtypes', 'HIV', and 'Tanzania' were used as key concepts alongside related search terms to construct the search strategy. Boolean operators 'AND', 'OR', and 'NOT' were used to combine different concepts, similar terms, and exclude studies","The paper does not mention the specific sequencing method used, focusing instead on the analysis of data from multiple studies."
40872801,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,The paper does not mention whether samples were cloned prior to sequencing.,"The systematic literature search was carried out between February and March 2025 on online databases including MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL, while Google Scholar was used to identify grey literature and would not be identified by other databases. The concepts 'Drug Resistance Mutations', 'Drug Resistance', 'ART resistance', 'HIV-1 Subtypes', 'HIV Subtypes', 'HIV', and 'Tanzania' were used as key concepts alongside related search terms to construct the search strategy. Boolean operators 'AND', 'OR', and 'NOT' were used to combine different concepts, similar terms, and exclude studies",The paper does not provide information on whether the samples were cloned before sequencing.
40872801,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,The paper does not specify the type of clinical samples that were sequenced.,"We searched studies that genotyped drug resistance mutations from clinical specimens collected from participants who were receiving Antiretroviral Therapy (ART) and who serum samples tested HIV positive,","The paper does not mention the specific clinical specimens that were sequenced, focusing instead on the overall prevalence of drug resistance mutations."
40872801,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, the paper reports sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen.","The overall prevalence of acquired drug resistance mutations in the participants with virological failure whose samples were successfully genotyped was 87.61% (95% CI: 76.25–95.91%, I2 = 96.15%).","The paper discusses the prevalence of drug resistance mutations in participants with virological failure, indicating that sequences were obtained from these individuals."
40872801,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the paper does not indicate that the patients were part of a clinical trial.","All included studies were observational studies, including a total of 9685 participants on ART.","The paper focuses on observational studies rather than clinical trials, indicating that the patients were not part of a clinical trial."
40872801,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,The paper mentions that the meta-analysis included studies with a total of 9685 participants on ART.,"All included studies were observational studies, including a total of 9685 participants on ART, whereby 6677 (68.94%) were women. Eight (34.78%) of included studies involved child participants, whereby a total of 2320 (23.95%) children were enrolled.",The paper states that the meta-analysis included studies with 9685 individuals wiith samples genotyped for for HIV sequencing.
40872801,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","To inform policy, this review aimed to determine the magnitude and patterns of DRMs in patients on ART in Tanzania. A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024. A total of 9685 HIV patients from 23 eligible studies were analyzed. The prevalence of virological failure in studies that used a threshold of >1000 and >400 copies/mL was 24.83% (95% CI: 17.85-32.53%) and 36.94% (95% CI: 24.79-50.00%), respectively. Major DRMs were observed at 87.61% (95% CI: 76.25-95.91%). A decrease in prevalence was observed in studies conducted from 2019, with a pooled prevalence of 62.15% (95% CI: 31.57-88.33%). The most frequently observed HIV-1 subtypes were subtype C at 36.20% (95% CI: 30.71-41.85%), A1 at 33.13% (95% CI: 28.23-38.20%), and subtype D at 16.00% (95% CI: 11.41-21.12%), while recombinant forms of the virus were observed at 13.29% (95% CI: 9.79-17.17%). The prevalence of DRMs against NRTIs and NNRTIs was significantly high, while that against INSTIs and PIs was low, supporting the continued use of PI- and INSTI-based regimens in Tanzania and the need for continued surveillance of DRMs.","The paper includes patients on ART, which indicates that they had previously received ARV drugs."
40872801,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,The paper reports the receipt of NRTIs and NNRTIs by individuals in the study before sample sequencing.,"The prevalence of DRMs against NRTisi and NNRTIs were significantly high, while that against INSTIs and PIs was low supporting the continued use of PI and INSTI-based regimens in Tanzania and the need for continued surveillance of DRMs",The paper mentions the presence of drug resistance mutation against INsti and PI drugs which indicates that individuals had received INSTIs and PIs.The also report the receipt of NRTIs and NNRTIs.
40872801,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The paper mentions the use of various NRTIs including 3TC, FTC, AZT, and TDF.","The most frequently observed NRTI drug resistance mutations (DRMs) were against 3TC and FTC, with high prevalence of M184V and M184I [19,37], and were attributed to the fact that these drugs have been mainstay of first-line regimens, while AZT and TDF monotherapy later followed, brought about by limited resources at that time [39]. Instiutional ട്രന് Mixed durg resistance to Abacavir with E142 and L28I were also observed owing to the fact that ABC was the only available drug in Tanzania at the time [2,38]. We should also highlight that the high levels of FTC and 3TC were linked to their enhanced susceptibiltyto other NRTIs [3,4].","The paper lists specific NRTIs that were commonly used in the regimens of the individuals included in the study, indicating which drugs were received prior to sequencing."
40872801,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"No, the paper does not mention that the sequences were made publicly available.",The systematic review protocol was registered in the International Prospective Register of Systematic Reviews (PROSPERO) on 7 January 2025 under the registration number CRD42025606698.,"The paper does not state that the sequences were made publicly available, focusing instead on the analysis of data from included studies."
40938120,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples. Specifically, it mentions that 1,048 sequences were included in the final analysis after applying quality control criteria.","In this study, we enrolled 1,260 newly diagnosed HIV-infected individuals. Among them, 1,159 pol gene sequences were successfully amplified. After applying quality control criteria, 1,048 sequences were included in the final analysis.","The study involved the collection and analysis of HIV sequences from patient samples, indicating that the sequences were derived from clinical specimens."
40938120,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"The paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data. It focuses on genetic drug resistance and epidemiological data, but does not mention functional assays or phenotypic susceptibility testing.","Molecular transmission networks provide critical insights into the dissemination pathways of drug-resistant HIV strains within populations. Studies from Croatia (13) and Mexico (14) have shown that resistant strains frequently circulate within tightly connected transmission networks. Similarly, the emergence of drug resistance clusters in certain epidemic regions of China indicates ongoing transmission of resistant HIV strains among PLWH (15, 16).
In Guangxi, molecular network studies on PDR have been conducted in several regions, including Qinzhou and Baise (2). This study revealed that individuals over the age of 50 were more likely to be part of transmission clusters (TCs) and that the CRF08_BC subtype was particularly prone to sharing drug resistance mutations (DRMs) (2). These findings highlight the urgent need to strengthen surveillance and implement targeted interventions. By addressing critical data gaps and advancing understanding of regional resistance dynamics, this study provided essential evidence to inform the design of targeted and effective treatment and prevention programs in Guangxi and other areas.","The paper primarily discusses genetic resistance and epidemiological factors, without presenting any in vitro susceptibility testing data."
40938120,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates are PX133190-PX134237.,HIV-1 sequence data generated in this study have been deposited in GenBank and are available under accession numbers PX133190-PX134237.,The paper explicitly states the GenBank accession numbers for the sequences generated in the study.
40938120,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The paper reports the sequencing of the pol gene, which includes the full-length protease (PR) and the first 299 codons of the RT gene.","An in-house RT nested PCR was used to amplify a 1,061 bp fragment of the pol gene, covering the full-length protease (PR, 99 codons) and the first 299 codons of the RT gene.","The sequencing method described in the materials and methods section indicates that the pol gene, including PR and RT, was sequenced."
40938120,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,"The sequenced samples were obtained from China, specifically Nanning City, Guangxi Province.","This study assessed the prevalence, associated factors, and transmission networks of PDR among newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals in Guangxi, China, from 2019 to 2022.","The study was conducted in Guangxi, China, and all samples were collected from this region."
40938120,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from 2019 to 2022.,"A cross-sectional survey using a convenience sampling method was conducted across the nine counties and districts of Nanning City, Guangxi Province, from 1 January 2019 to 31 December 2022.",The study period is clearly stated as 2019 to 2022.
40938120,7,What method was used for sequencing?,"The method used for sequencing was Sanger sequencing, conducted by Sangon Biotech using the Applied Biosystems 3730XL Genetic Analyzer.","PCR products were confirmed by agarose gel electrophoresis, and positive amplicons were sequenced by Sangon Biotech (Shanghai, China) using the Applied Biosystems 3730XL Genetic Analyzer.",The paper describes the use of Sanger sequencing for determining the sequences of the amplified HIV DNA.
40938120,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the samples were not cloned prior to sequencing. The paper does not mention any cloning of samples.","PCR products were confirmed by agarose gel electrophoresis, and positive amplicons were sequenced by Sangon Biotech (Shanghai, China) using the Applied Biosystems 3730XL Genetic Analyzer.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
40938120,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma samples were sequenced in this study. HIV-1 RNA was extracted from plasma samples for sequencing.,"HIV-1 RNA was extracted from plasma samples using the High Pure Viral RNA Kit (Roche, Germany).",The paper specifies that HIV-1 RNA was extracted from plasma samples for sequencing.
40938120,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"No, the study focused on newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals, so no sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen.","A cross-sectional study was conducted between 2019 and 2022 in Nanning, Guangxi, involving 1,260 newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals with HIV.","The study specifically targeted newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals, indicating that the sequences were not from individuals with virological failure."
40938120,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the study was a cross-sectional survey and did not involve a clinical trial setting.","This study aimed to investigate the prevalence of primary PDR and to explore the transmission factors of DRM within molecular networks by recruiting newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals, thereby providing essential evidence to inform and enhance HIV control strategies.",The study was a cross-sectional survey and not a clinical trial.
40938120,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,"Samples were obtained from 1,260 individuals for HIV sequencing.","A cross-sectional study was conducted between 2019 and 2022 in Nanning, Guangxi, involving 1,260 newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals with HIV.","The paper states that 1,260 newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals were recruited for the study, indicating the number of individuals from whom samples were obtained."
40938120,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"No, the paper does not report sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs, as it focused on newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals.","A cross-sectional study was conducted between 2019 and 2022 in Nanning, Guangxi, involving 1,260 newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals with HIV.","The study specifically targeted newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals, indicating that the sequences were not from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs."
40938120,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The study did not have individuals who received antiretroviral drugs before sample sequencing, as it focused on newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals.","A cross-sectional study was conducted between 2019 and 2022 in Nanning, Guangxi, involving 1,260 newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals with HIV.","The study specifically targeted newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals, indicating that they had not received ARV drugs before sample sequencing."
40938120,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The study did not have individuals who received antiretroviral drugs before sample sequencing, as it focused on newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals.","A cross-sectional study was conducted between 2019 and 2022 in Nanning, Guangxi, involving 1,260 newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals with HIV.","The study specifically targeted newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals, indicating that they had not received ARV drugs before sample sequencing."
40938120,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"Yes, the sequences were made publicly available and are listed under specific GenBank accession numbers.",HIV-1 sequence data generated in this study have been deposited in GenBank and are available under accession numbers PX133190-PX134237.,"The paper states that the sequence data were deposited in GenBank, indicating they were made publicly available."
40938996,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"No, the paper does not report HIV sequences from patient samples.",We conducted long-term propagation experiments with increasing DTG concentrations in peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs).,The study focuses on sequences obtained from laboratory experiments rather than directly from patient samples.
40938996,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"Yes, the paper reports in vitro drug susceptibility data.","As an additional approach to measuring the level of DTG resistance conferred by the NC mutations in the SupT1 T cell line, we performed single-cycle DTG sensitivity assays using a vesicular stomatitis virus G (VSV-G)-pseudotyped HIV-1 nanoLuc reporter virus (Fig. 1, C and D).",The inclusion of single-cycle DTG sensitivity assays suggests that drug susceptibility data was generated.
40938996,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers.,"""The HIV-1 integration site analysis using 2-LTR circles and the DNA end integrity analysis were performed using our previously described bioinformatic pipeline (63). The FASTQ files were prepared by being converted to their reverse complements using Seqtk (https://github.com/lh3/seqtk) to accommodate the input requirement of the previously described pipeline (63).""",The study focuses on experimental results and does not mention depositing sequences in GenBank.
40938996,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,The study reported sequencing of the NC and IN genes.,"Here, we show that these NC mutations accelerate the kinetics of viral DNA integration, suggesting that they limit the window of time available for INSTIs to block viral DNA integration.",The focus on NC and IN genes is evident from the discussion on their mutations and effects.
40938996,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The paper does not specify the countries of origin for the sequenced samples.,Abstract. IMPORTANT: All of our DTG selection experiments were performed using PBMCs infected with HIV-1 isolates from PWH at the NIH Clinic per the study protocol [1].,"The study does not mention the geographical origin of the samples, indicating they were laboratory-derived."
40938996,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The paper does not provide specific years for when the sequenced samples were obtained.,Our previous study demonstrated that HIV-1 frequently acquires NC mutations in the presence of DTG independent of viral strain (49).,The focus is on experimental mutations rather than the timeline of sample collection.
40938996,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The paper mentions using Sanger sequencing for some methods.,The 2-LTR junction sequence was determined by Sanger sequencing (Poochon Scientific) using the M13 reverse primer.,Mention of Sanger sequencing indicates the method used.
40938996,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,The paper does not mention whether samples were cloned prior to sequencing.,"The analysis indicated that the selected NC mutations in the zinc finger domain do not affect Gag processing in virus-producing cells or in virions (fig. S2, B to E), virus release efficiency (fig. S2F), or the amount of virion-associated RT protein (p66/p51) (fig. S2G).","The study does not mention sample cloning, focusing on direct sequencing methods."
40938996,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) were sequenced.,We conducted long-term propagation experiments with increasing DTG concentrations in peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs).,The focus on PBMCs as the source of samples is clear from the context.
40938996,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"The paper discusses virological failure in the context of experiments, not individual patient data.",Persons with HIV (PWH) receiving integrase (IN) strand transfer inhibitors (INSTIs) have been reported to experience virologic failure (VF) in the absence of resistance mutations in IN. We previously reported that mutations in the viral nucleocapsid (NC) are selected in the presence of the INSTI dolutegravir (DTG).,"The discussion on virological failure is within experimental contexts, not patient histories."
