41056006,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No.,"Emergence of LEN resistance was an exploratory endpoint. HIV-1 capsid genotypic and phenotypic data were assessed at study entry using the GenoSure Gag-Pro and PhenoSense Gag-Pro assays (Monogram Biosciences). Resistance testing was performed for any participants who met one of the following virologic failure criteria: suboptimal virological response, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL and a decline of <1log10 from Day 1 to Week 10; virological rebound, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL after reaching <50 copies/mL, or two consecutive visits with an increase from nadir of >1log10; or participants with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL at last study visit.",The paper does not mention in vitro drug susceptibility testing. The focus is on clinical outcomes and resistance mutations in vivo.
