41056006,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,Yes.,"CALIBRATE was a Phase 2, randomized, open-label study (NCT04143594).",The study was a clinical trial evaluating the efficacy and safety of lenacapavir.
41056006,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,Not applicable.,"Total number of participants who ·experienced virologic failure 10 (6%), participants who experienced treatment-emergent LEN RAMs, n=4; 3 of these occurrences have been reported elsewhere. After Week 80, participants in TG4 completed the study. Participants in TG1-TG3 could continue on their assigned treatment from Week 80 onwards and attend clinic visits alternating between every 10 and every 16 weeks until the product became accessible through an access programme, or until the study sponsor elected to discontinue the study in the country. Participants in TG1 and TG2 required oral bridging if an SC injection of LEN could not be administered within the protocol visit window; results from these participants have been reported elsewhere. In this study, participants received LEN with asynchronously dosed ARVs, which may be associated with the development of resistance.",The study did not report obtaining samples specifically for HIV sequencing.
