41057785,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Participants received NRTI, NNRTI, PI, or INSTI drug classes before sample sequencing.","Table 1 Demographic and clinical characteristics

Participants had a mean age of 28.0 years, 11.2 years on ART, and DRMs detected in  59.6. Mutation prevalence was NNRTIs (52.8), NRTIs (50.2), PI major (25.5), and INSTI (c 0.9). Key drug class mutations included, NNRTIs (K103KN25.1, G190AS14.0, Y181CF/V/F12.3), NRTIs (M184V45.0, T215FY30.2, M41L18.3), PIs (M46I15.7, V82VA12.3, I54LV9.4), and INSTIs (E138K, T66A, G118R, E92EV all at 0.4).","The treatment regimens included various combinations of NRTI, NNRTI, PI, and INSTI drugs, indicating the classes received."
41057785,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Specific drugs received included ABC, AZT, D4T, TDF, DTG, DRV, ETR, LPV, and RAL.","Results Participants had a mean age of 28.0 years, 11.2 years on ART, and DRMs detected in  9.6. Mutation prevalence was NNRTIs (52.8), NRTIs (50.2), PI major (25.5), and INSTI (c 0.9). Key drug class mutations included, NNRTIs (K103KN25.1, G190AS14.0, Y181CF/V/F12.3), NRTIs (M184V45.0, T215FY30.2, M41L18.3), PIs (M46I15.7, V82VA12.3, I54LV9.4), and INSTIs (E138K, T66A, G118R, E92EV all at 0.4). DRMs were significantly associated with longer time (months) to virological failure: NRTIs (129.3 vs. 88.2, p = 0.008), NNRTIs (127.4 vs. 84.2, p = 0.003), and PIs (170.9 vs. 88.7, p = 0.000). In cox regression analysis, time to virological failure was significantly associated with age (HR: 0.987; CI: 0.976-0.998; p = 0.019, aHR: 0.976; CI: 0.959-0.993; p = 0.007), ART duration (HR: 0.828; CI: 0.800-0.856; p = 0.000, aHR: 0.827; CI: 0.792-0.863; p = 0.000), drug mutations; NRTI (HR: 0.659; CI: 0.484-0.898; p = 0.008), NNRTI (HR: 0.628; CI: 0.463-0.851; p = 0.003), and PI (HR: 0.257; CI: 0.146-0.453; p = 0.000, aHR: 0.337; CI: 0.137-0.831; p = 0.018).","Although the specific drugs taken by participants before sample sequencing is not mentioned, the ART types and most taken drugs at initiation is mentioned in the manuscript."
41057785,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,The paper does not mention whether the sequences were made publicly available.,"Methods This cohort study retrospectively reviewed medical records of 235 People living with HIV (PLHIV) who underwent HIV drug resistance testing at the Mildmay Uganda Hospital (MUgH) from 2018 to 2023. Data on demographics, ART, and DRMs were analyzed. Kaplan-Meier and log-rank tests were used to compare median time to virological failure. Cox proportional hazards models assessed associations factors associated with time to virological failure, with significance set at  \(p < 0.05\) .","The study does not mention the public availability of sequences, focusing instead on the clinical and resistance data."
41088231,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples.","The near full-length genome (NFLG) of HIV-1 was amplified with two overlapping segments by the near endpoint dilution method. The individual (230794) was 47 years old and got infected via heterosexual contact in Guangzhou City, Guangdong Province. Specimen 230794 was collected in Oct. 2023 from a 47-year-old man who claimed to have contracted HIV-1 through heterosexual contact in Guangzhou City, Guangdong Province, China.","The paper describes the収 collection and sequencing of HIV-1 from a patient sample, specifically mentioning the individual and the circumstances of infection."
41088231,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","No major/accessory mutations conferring resistance to PIs, NRTIs, NNRTIs, or INSTIs were identified, therefore, the strain 230794 was susceptible to 26 drugs in four categories (as shown in Supplementary Table 2). However, the strain 230794 harbors an INSTI other mutation, L74I, which is highly polymorphic and is not more common in individuals receiving INSTIs than in INSTI-naive individuals.",The paper discusses drug susceptibility in terms of genetic mutations but does not mention any in vitro testing of drug susceptibility.
41088231,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The GenBank accession number for sequenced HIV isolates is PV187006.,The NFLG sequence of strain 230794 was obtained and submitted to GenBank (accession number PV187006).,The paper explicitly states that the sequence was submitted to GenBank with this accession number.
41088231,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The near full-length genome (NFLG) of HIV-1 was sequenced, covering multiple genes.","The near full-length genome (NFLG) of HIV-1 was amplified with two overlapping segments by the near endpoint dilution method. The NFLG sequence of strain 230794 was 8260 nucleotides (nt) in length, with two CRF02_AG segments substituting in the backbone of subtype F2 in the vif and env gene regions.","The paper mentions the sequencing of the near full-length genome, which includes multiple genes and regions."
41088231,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from China.,"In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.","The paper specifies that the sample was collected in Guangdong Province, China."
41088231,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained in 2023 and 2025.,"Specimen 230794 was collected in Oct. 2023 from a 47-year-old man who claimed to have contracted HIV-1 through heterosexual contact in Guangzhou City, Guangdong Province, China. Proviral DNA was extracted from the whole-blood sample collected in 2025 with the Viral DNA Extraction Kit (Supbio, China).",The paper mentions the collection years of the samples used for sequencing.
41088231,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The sequencing method used was Sanger sequencing.,"Positive products were directly purified and sequenced by Sangon Biotech (Shanghai) Co., Ltd with Sanger sequencing method. The NFLG was assembled and cleaned by the software Sequencher V5.1 (Gene Codes, United States).",The paper explicitly states that the sequencing was done using the Sanger method.
41088231,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the samples were not cloned prior to sequencing.","Positive products were directly purified and sequenced by Sangon Biotech (Shanghai) Co., Ltd with Sanger sequencing method.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
41088231,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma and whole-blood samples were sequenced.,"Viral RNA was extracted from the 2023 plasma sample using a magnetic bead-based method. Proviral DNA was extracted from the whole-blood sample collected in 2025 with the Viral DNA Extraction Kit (Supbio, China).",The paper specifies that both plasma and whole-blood samples were used for sequencing.
41088231,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"No, the paper does not report sequences from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen.","In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.",The paper mentions the  the patient was not on ART at the time of sample collection and was not mentioned the virological failure.
41088231,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the paper does not mention that the patients were in a clinical trial.","The study was approved by the institutional review board of Guangzhou Eighth People's Hospital (No. 202353290), and the individual provided written informed consent. In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.",The paper does not mention any clinical trial involvement for the patients.
41088231,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,One individual had samples obtained for HIV sequencing.,"In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.",The paper specifically mentions the sequencing of samples from one individual.
41088231,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"No, the paper focuses on antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals.","In the previous drug resistance surveillance among 5602 HIV-1-infected antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naive individuals in Guangdong Province from Jan. 2023 to Dec. 2023, we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F2 and CRF02_AG, two subtypes of HIV that are very rare in China and even worldwide.",The paper specifically mentions the inclusion of ART-naïve individuals in the study.
