41093949,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"No, the paper does not report HIV sequences from patient samples.","The same RTI-induced DRMs were introduced into infectious clones of subtypes B and CRF01_AE, and phenotypic resistance tests were performed to compare the differences in susceptibilities to various RTIs.",The study focuses on in vitro phenotypic resistance testing using infectious clones rather than patient-derived sequences.
41093949,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"Yes, the paper reports in vitro drug susceptibility data.","Phenotypic resistance results were obtained in this experiment were in general agreement with the predictions of the Stanford HIV resistance database, but there were still notable inconsistencies.",The paper includes detailed in vitro phenotypic susceptibility testing of various drugs against different HIV-1 subtypes.
41093949,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates are PQ735970-PQ735985.,The NCBI repository accession numbers for the AE/B recombinants are: PQ735970-PQ735985.,The paper explicitly lists these accession numbers in the results section.
