41112839,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples.","A total of 237 samples from different patients were analyzed, and 131 (55.3%) were successfully amplified and sequenced.",The paper indicates that HIV sequences were obtained from samples collected from patients in various regions.
41112839,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","Methods: A pretreatment drug resistance survey was carried out in 35 sites throughout the country between 2017 and 2018 using dried blood spots and whole blood samples. Amplification and sequencing were performed on the partial reverse transcriptase (RT) gene using the Agence Nationale de Recherches sur le Sida et les hepatitis virales (ANRS: French National Agency for Research on acquired immunodeficiency syndrome [AIDS] and Viral Hepatitis)/AC11 method at the HIV National Reference Laboratory. Surveillance drug resistance mutations (SDRM) were analyzed using the Calibrated Population Resistance v8.1, and the proportion of SDRM was evaluated after grouping sites by geographical areas.",The focus of the paper is on genotyping and surveillance drug resistance mutations rather than on in vitro drug susceptibility testing.
41112839,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates are PP280627 to PP280757.,The RT-generated sequences were deposited in the National Institutes of Health GenBank database under accession numbers PP280627 to PP280757.,The paper explicitly states that the sequences were deposited in GenBank with these accession numbers.
41112839,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,The partial reverse transcriptase (RT) gene was sequenced.,Amplification and sequencing were performed on the partial reverse transcriptase (RT) gene using the Agence Nationale de Recherches sur le Sida et les hepatitis virales (ANRS: French National Agency for Research on acquired immunodeficiency syndrome [AIDS] and Viral Hepatitis)/AC11 method at the HIV National Reference Laboratory.,The paper mentions sequencing the partial RT gene.
41112839,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from Senegal.,HIV-1 genetic diversity and pretreatment drug resistance survey prior to dolutegravir introduction in Senegal,The study was conducted as a pretreatment drug resistance survey in Senegal.
41112839,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained between 2017 and 2018.,PDR surveillance was carried out between 2017 and 2018 according to WHO recommendations.,The paper states that the surveillance was conducted during these years.
41112839,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sequencing was performed using the Big Dye Terminator v3.1 method and ABI 3100 Avant sequencer.,"Purified and quantified polymerase chain reaction products were sequenced by using Big Dye Terminator v3.1 (Life Technologies, Courtaboeuf, France), and electrophoresis was performed on the ABI 3100 Avant sequencer (Applied Biosystems, France) as previously described.",The paper provides details on the sequencing method used.
41112839,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the paper does not mention that samples were cloned prior to sequencing.","From 200µl of plasma or two spots of DBS, HIV-1 viral ribonucleic acid (RNA) was extracted on the Nuclisens easyMAG® platform (Biomerieux, France) according to the manufacturer’s recommendations. The resulting RNA was used to synthesize complementary deoxyribonucleic acid (cDNA), which was amplified using the ANRS AC11 genotyping technique targeting the first 240 amino acids of RT.",The paper describes the preparation and direct sequencing of clinical specimens without cloning.
41112839,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Both dried blood spots (DBS) and plasma samples were sequenced.,A total of 221 DBS and 17 plasma samples were analyzed. The amplification success rate was 55% for DBS (121/221) and 58.8% for plasma (10/17).,The paper specifies that these types of samples were used for sequencing.
41112839,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"No, the paper focused on antiretroviral therapy-naive patients.","Objectives: This study aimed to document the prevalence of pretreatment drug resistance in antiretroviral therapy-naive patients in Senegal, describe mutation profiles, and evaluate their potential impact on future therapy.",The paper specifically targeted ART-naive patients for the survey.
41112839,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial.","The inclusion criteria for patients in the sites were to be HIV-1-positive men or women, aged at least 18, ART-naive (defined as never having received any antiretroviral therapy, including prevention of mother-to-child transmission [PMTCT] regimens), and newly diagnosed based on the patient and the healthcare provider declarations.",The paper describes a surveillance study rather than a clinical trial.
41112839,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,Samples were obtained from 331 antiretroviral therapy-naive patients.,"The final selection was made using WHO randomization software, which resulted in the selection of 35 sites throughout the country for surveillance of PDR, with a target of 331 patients to be included.",The paper mentions that the target number of patients for inclusion was 331.
41112839,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"No, the paper focused on antiretroviral therapy-naive patients.","Objectives: This study aimed to document the prevalence of pretreatment drug resistance in antiretroviral therapy-naive patients in Senegal, describe mutation profiles, and evaluate their potential impact on future therapy.",The paper specifically targeted ART-naive patients for the survey.
41112839,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The individuals were antiretroviral therapy-naive, so no drug classes were received before sampling.","Objectives: This study aimed to document the prevalence of pretreatment drug resistance in antiretroviral therapy-naive patients in Senegal, describe mutation profiles, and evaluate their potential impact on future therapy.",The paper specifically targeted ART-naive patients for the survey.
41112839,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"The individuals were antiretroviral therapy-naive, so no specific drugs were received before sampling.","Objectives: This study aimed to document the prevalence of pretreatment drug resistance in antiretroviral therapy-naive patients in Senegal, describe mutation profiles, and evaluate their potential impact on future therapy.",The paper specifically targeted ART-naive patients for the survey.
41112839,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"Yes, the sequences were deposited in the National Institutes of Health GenBank database.",The RT-generated sequences were deposited in the National Institutes of Health GenBank database under accession numbers PP280627 to PP280757.,The paper explicitly states that the sequences were deposited in GenBank.
41129268,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples. Specifically, it mentions that 333 samples were successfully genotyped for drug resistance mutations.","Methods: We identified CLHIV aged 0-15 years experiencing virologic failure on first-line antiretroviral therapy (ART) in Uganda between January-November 2021 from the Central Public Health Laboratory database. Remnant viral load samples were tested for HIVDR using Sanger sequencing. Results: Among 333 successfully genotyped patient samples, 122 (36.6%) CLHIV were on a DTG-based regimen and 136 (40.8%) on a lopinavir-based regimen.","The methods section outlines the identification and testing of patient samples for HIV drug resistance, confirming the sequencing of HIV from these samples."
41129268,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"Yes, the paper reports in vitro drug susceptibility data based on Sanger sequencing results.","Methods: We identified CLHIV aged 0-15 years experiencing virologic failure on first-line antiretroviral therapy (ART) in Uganda between January-November 2021 from the Central Public Health Laboratory database. Remnant viral load samples were tested for HIVDR using Sanger sequencing. Drug resistance mutations (DRMs) were identified and antiretroviral susceptibility was interpreted using the Stanford University HIVDR Database algorithms. Results: Drug susceptibility analysis revealed that the majority of CLHIV (78.7%, 262/333) had clinically significant resistance (intermediate-to-high level drug resistance) to at least one ARV.","The paper discusses the interpretation of drug resistance mutations and the susceptibility profiles of the antiretroviral drugs, indicating the presence of drug susceptibility data."
41129268,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates.,No evidence,"The content of the paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, indicating that this information was not included."
41129268,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The paper mentions sequencing for drug resistance mutations primarily in the reverse transcriptase, protease, and integrase genes.","Frequencies of DRMs were calculated overall and stratified by drug class of the mutation, including mutations against NRTIs, NNRTIs, protease inhibitors (PIs), and integrase inhibitors (INSTIs).","The paper discusses the identification of drug resistance mutations across various classes, which corresponds to the respective genes sequenced."
41129268,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from Uganda.,Methods: We identified CLHIV aged 0-15 years experiencing virologic failure on first-line antiretroviral therapy (ART) in Uganda between January-November 2021 from the Central Public Health Laboratory database.,"The study was conducted in Uganda, and all samples were collected from ART-accredited health facilities in the country."
41129268,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained between January and November 2021.,Methods: We identified CLHIV aged 0-15 years experiencing virologic failure on first-line antiretroviral therapy (ART) in Uganda between January-November 2021 from the Central Public Health Laboratory database.,The methods section clearly states the time frame during which the samples were collected.
41129268,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The paper used Sanger sequencing technology for sequencing.,"Methods: Remnant viral load samples were tested for HIVDR using Sanger sequencing. Once a sample was referred to the HIVDR laboratory, clinicians received email notifications from the HIVDR Database to upload their clients’ social, psychosocial, and medical profiles into the database.",The methods section explicitly mentions the use of Sanger sequencing technology for testing the samples.
41129268,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, the samples were not cloned prior to sequencing.","Methods: Remnant viral load samples were tested for HIVDR using Sanger sequencing. Once a sample was referred to the HIVDR laboratory, clinicians received email notifications from the HIVDR Database to upload their clients’ social, psychosocial, and medical profiles into the database.","The methods section does not mention any cloning of samples, indicating that this step was not performed."
41129268,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma samples were sequenced.,"Data for this analysis came from previously collected VL samples from children aged ≤15 years of age on first-line ART enrolled in any ART-accredited health facility in Uganda whose VL sample satisfied the following criteria: (1) sample tested for VL between January and November 2021, (2) sample type was plasma (3) VF defined as VL ≥1000 copies/mL for children on EFV or NVP or repeat VL >1000 copies/ml for children on Lopinavir/ritonavir (LPV/r) or DTG.","The methods section specifies that VL samples were plasma samples, confirming the type of clinical specimens sequenced."
41129268,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, the paper reports sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on their treatment regimen.",We identified CLHIV aged 0-15 years experiencing virologic failure on first-line antiretroviral therapy (ART) in Uganda between January-November 2021 from the Central Public Health Laboratory database.,The study focused on children living with HIV experiencing virologic failure on first-line antiretroviral therapy.
41129268,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the patients were not in a clinical trial; the study was a routine data collection as part of standard of care.",Methods: We identified CLHIV aged 0-15 years experiencing virologic failure on first-line antiretroviral therapy (ART) in Uganda between January-November 2021 from the Central Public Health Laboratory database.,The context of the study indicates that it was a standard care initiative rather than a clinical trial.
41129268,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,Samples were obtained from 333 individuals for HIV sequencing.,"Results: Among 333 successfully genotyped patient samples, 122 (36.6%) CLHIV were on a DTG-based regimen and 136 (40.8%) on a lopinavir-based regimen.","The results section states that 333 samples were successfully genotyped, indicating the number of individuals from whom samples were obtained."
41129268,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","Among 333 CLHIV with successful sample amplification, 61 (18.3%) were aged 1-4 years, 79 (23.7%) aged 5-9 years, 89 (26.7%) aged 10-12 years, and 104 (31.2%) aged 13-15 years. There were 101 (30.3%) CLHIV taking ART for less than five years, 104 (31.2%) taking ART 5-9 years, and 128 (38.4%) taking ART 10 or more years.",The demographic section describes children previously taking ARV drugs.
41129268,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Individuals received drugs from the NRTI, NNRTI, PI, and INSTI classes before sample sequencing.","Frequencies of DRMs were calculated overall and stratified by drug class of the mutation, including mutations against NRTIs, NNRTIs, protease inhibitors (PIs), and integrase inhibitors (INSTIs).","The paper discusses the presence of drug resistance mutations across these drug classes, indicating prior receipt of these drugs."
41129268,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Drugs received included Dolutegravir, Abacavir, Zidovudine, Tenofovir, Lopinavir, Lamivudine, Darunavir, Efavirenz, and Nevirapine.","Demographic and clinical variables explored included sex, age category, duration of time on ART, reported level of adherence to ART (good, fair, or poor), VL category at sample collection (defined as VL < 10,000, VL 10,000-100,000, and VL>100,000), and regimen at sample collection. DTG regimen, 122 (36.6%) DTG; LPV regimen, 136 (40.8%) NVP regimen, 33 (9.9%) EFV regimen  41 (12.3%) Other regimen, 1 (0.4%).",The results section lists the specific drugs that were part of the treatment regimens prior to sample sequencing.
41129268,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"No, the paper does not mention that the sequences were made publicly available.",No evidence,"The content of the paper does not mention any public availability of the sequences, indicating that this was not addressed."
41130593,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"Yes, the paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples.",Resistance to LEN was detected in 0 of 2134 participants (P1) and 2 of 2179 participants (P2); both developed N74D.,"The paper discusses resistance analyses from the PURPOSE trials, indicating that HIV-1 sequences were obtained from patient samples for genotyping resistance mutations."
41130593,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.",Phenotyping of the clinical isolates in the PURPOSE trials was not attempted; no susceptibility data were available.,"The focus of the paper is on clinical outcomes and resistance mutations observed in patient samples, rather than in vitro susceptibility testing."
41130593,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates are not provided in the paper.,No specific GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates were mentioned in the text.,The paper does not include any references to GenBank accession numbers for the sequences analyzed.
41130593,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The HIV genes sequenced include capsid, protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase.","Upon HIV-1 diagnosis, plasma samples were collected for HIV-1 RNA quantification and resistance analyses. Samples with HIV-1 RNA ≥200 copies/mL were analyzed for genotypic resistance in the HIV-1 CA, protease (PR), reverse transcriptase (RT), and integrase coding regions using the GenoSure® GAG PRO and GenoSure PRIme® assays.",The paper describes the genotyping of these specific genes for resistance analysis.
41130593,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,"The sequenced samples were obtained from multiple countries, including South Africa.",The LEN resistance-associated mutation K70R was also detected in one South African participant with a subtype C virus and no exposure to LEN. This is likely a rare polymorphism.,The paper mentions the detection of a LEN resistance-associated mutation in a participant from South Africa.
41130593,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The specific years from which the sequenced samples were obtained are not provided in the paper.,No specific years for sample collection were mentioned in the text.,The paper does not include detailed timelines for when the samples were collected.
41130593,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Next-generation sequencing (NGS) was used for sequencing.,"Genotypic CA resistance testing at Monogram was conducted using a next-generation sequencing platform (MiSeq; Illumina), with reporting of mutants present in ≥10% of sequences obtained for a given sample.",The paper specifies that NGS was the method used for detecting resistance mutations.
41130593,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"No, samples were not cloned prior to sequencing.","Genotypic CA resistance testing at Monogram was conducted using a next-generation sequencing platform (MiSeq; Illumina),",The paper describes the use of NGS without mentioning any cloning of samples.
41130593,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma samples were sequenced.,"Upon HIV-1 diagnosis, plasma samples were collected for HIV-1 RNA quantification and resistance analyses.",The paper mentions that plasma samples were collected and analyzed for resistance.
41130593,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"Yes, sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure.","Participant A harbored the substitution M184M/I in RT at HIV-1 diagnosis (Week 26). Adherence was low at Week 4, improved by Week 13, then declined near the time of HIV-1 acquisition (Figure 2; Supplementary Table 2). Virologic suppression could not be confirmed although the final viral load was < 200 copies/mL (Supplementary Table 3).",The paper discusses participants who experienced virological failure and had resistance mutations.
41130593,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"Yes, the patients were part of clinical trials.","The PURPOSE trials assessed the efficacy of LEN and emtricitabine/tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (F/TDF) in cisgender women (PURPOSE 1; P1) and in cisgender men, transgender women, transgender men and gender nonbinary persons (PURPOSE 2; P2).",The paper details the clinical trials (PURPOSE 1 and 2) from which the data were obtained.
41130593,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,A total of 53 individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing in the resistance analysis population (RAP).,Tested for Resistance 37 in F/TAF; 16 in F/TDF Table 1. Study Disposition and Resistance Testing. O 43.068; Participants who acquired HIV-1 classified as Resistance Analysis. 51 in F/TDF—5 not Genotype,The paper mentions the number of participants tested for resistance in the various treatment groups.
41130593,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.",Participants who received study drug at Day 1 but were later found to have acquired HIV-1 before study initiation were also analyzed for resistance.,The paper discusses participants who were on ARV drugs and had their samples analyzed for resistance.
41130593,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Participants received NRTIs and INSTIs before sample sequencing.,"Virologic suppression (HIV-1 RNA < 50 copies/mL) was achieved on dolutegravir (DTG)/lamivudine (3TC)/TDF within 9 weeks of HIV-1 acquisition. DTG, dolutegravir; 3TC, lamivudine; TDF, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate;",The drugs mentioned in the context of achieving virological suppression were from these classes.
41130593,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Drugs received include tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF), lamivudine (3TC), and dolutegravir (DTG).",Virologic suppression (HIV-1 RNA < 50 copies/mL) was achieved on dolutegravir (DTG)/lamivudine (3TC)/TDF within 9 weeks of HIV-1 acquisition.,The paper specifically mentions these drugs as part of the treatment regimens before sample sequencing.
41130593,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,The paper does not mention whether the sequences were made publicly available.,No mention was made regarding the public availability of the sequences.,The paper does not provide information on whether the sequences were deposited in a public database.
41140464,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"No, the paper reports sequences retrieved from public databases, not direct patient samples.","We retrieved 7614 HIV-1 pol gene sequences, deposited between 2015 and 2025 from the Los Alamos HIV databases.","The study employed a meta-analysis approach using publicly available data, indicating that the sequences were not obtained directly from patient samples."
41140464,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"No, the paper does not report in vitro drug susceptibility data.","The Genetic Diversity and Drug Resistance Patterns of HIV-1 Pol Gene in East Africa. Assessment of DRMs in PR, RT, and IN Regions. Identification and classification of mutations associated with drug resistance in the PR, RT, and IN regions of the pol gene were carried out using the Stanford University HIV Drug Resistance Database (https://hivdb.stanford.edu/).","The study focused on the analysis of drug resistance mutations (DRMs) in sequences from a public database, without conducting in vitro susceptibility testing."
41140464,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates.,The paper mentions that sequences were retrieved from the Los Alamos National Laboratory (LANL) HIV Database and does not list specific GenBank accession numbers.,The study retrieved sequences from a database without providing individual accession numbers.
41140464,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"The paper reports sequencing of the pol gene, including PR, RT, and IN regions.","Data on HIV-1 pol gene sequences were retrieved from public database. Using appertaining software, the sequences were analyzed for assessment of DRMs in the pol gene enzymes (PR, RT, and IN).","The study specifically mentions the analysis of DRMs in the PR, RT, and IN regions of the pol gene."
41140464,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,"The sequenced samples were obtained from Kenya, Uganda, Tanzania, and Ethiopia.","We retrieved 7614 HIV-1 pol gene sequences, deposited between 2015 and 2025 from the Los Alamos HIV databases. The sequences were sourced from four EA countries: Kenya, Uganda, Tanzania, and Ethiopia.",The paper states that the sequences were retrieved from these four East African countries.
41140464,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained between 2015 and 2025.,"We retrieved 7614 HIV-1 pol gene sequences, deposited between 2015 and 2025 from the Los Alamos HIV databases.",The paper specifies that the sequences were deposited between these years.
41140464,7,What method was used for sequencing?,The specific method used for sequencing is not mentioned in the paper.,"The paper does not detail the sequencing methodology, focusing instead on the analysis of sequences retrieved from a database.","The study does not provide details on the sequencing methods, as it analyzed previously collected data."
41140464,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,The paper does not mention if samples were cloned prior to sequencing.,"The paper does not provide details on whether the samples were cloned, focusing instead on the analysis of sequences from a database.","The study does not mention any cloning of samples, as it used sequences retrieved from a database."
